            "body": "1. **Galti 1: \"Phenolphthalein rangheen hai, to ghol pakka Acid hi hoga\" maan lena.**\n   Phenolphthalein **Acid** mein bhi rangheen rehta hai aur **Neutral (shuddh paani)** mein bhi rangheen rehta hai! Isliye sirf phenolphthalein ke rangheen rehne se ye sabit hota hai ki ghol **Base nahi hai**, par Acid aur Neutral mein farq karne ke liye blue litmus ya methyl orange chahiye.\n2. **Galti 2: Haldi ke rang-badlav ko ulta likhna.**\n   Haldi **Base** mein laal-bhoori hoti hai, Acid mein nahi! Acid mein haldi apna asali **peela** rang hi rakhti hai.\n3. **Galti 3: Olfactory indicators mein \"Base mein gandh rehti hai\" likh dena.**\n   Bilkul ulta! Pyaaz, vanilla aur clove oil — teeno ki gandh **Acid mein bani rehti hai** aur **Base (jaise NaOH) mein gayab ho jaati hai**.\n4. **Galti 4: Litmus ka asali (neutral) rang neela ya laal samajhna.**\n   Lichen se nikle litmus ka asali neutral rang **baingani (purple)** hota hai. Blue aur Red litmus papers to lab ki suvidha ke liye pehle se rang kar banaye jaate hain.\n5. **Galti 5: Lab mein kisi ghol ko chakh kar ya ungli dubokar dekhna.**\n   Lab ke acids aur bases tez corrosive hote hain; unhe kabhi chakhna ya nange haath se chhuna nahi chahiye.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. **Galti 1: \"Phenolphthalein rangheen hai, to ghol pakka Acid hi hoga\" maan lena.**\n   Phenolphthalein **Acid** mein bhi rangheen rehta hai aur **Neutral (shuddh paani)** mein bhi rangheen rehta hai! Isliye sirf phenolphthalein ke rangheen rehne se ye sabit hota hai ki ghol **Base nahi hai**, par Acid aur Neutral mein farq karne ke liye blue litmus ya methyl orange chahiye.\n2. **Galti 2: Haldi ke rang-badlav ko ulta likhna.**\n   Haldi **Base** mein laal-bhoori hoti hai, Acid mein nahi! Acid mein haldi apna asali **peela** rang hi rakhti hai.\n3. **Galti 3: Olfactory indicators mein \"Base mein gandh rehti hai\" likh dena.**\n   Bilkul ulta! Pyaaz, vanilla aur clove oil — teeno ki gandh **Acid mein bani rehti hai** aur **Base (jaise NaOH) mein gayab ho jaati hai**.\n4. **Galti 4: Litmus ka asali (neutral) rang neela ya laal samajhna.**\n   Lichen se nikle litmus ka asali neutral rang **baingani (purple)** hota hai. Blue aur Red litmus papers to lab ki suvidha ke liye pehle se rang kar banaye jaate hain.\n5. **Galti 5: Lab mein kisi ghol ko chakh kar ya ungli dubokar dekhna.**\n   Lab ke acids aur bases tez corrosive hote hain; unhe kabhi chakhna ya nange haath se chhuna nahi chahiye."
