            "headingHinglish": "Alibaug ke namak ke khet aur rasoi ke pakodon ka raaz",
            "body": "Garmiyon ki chhuttiyon mein **Ketaki** apne chacha **Mr. Borgaonkar** ke saath Alibaug ke samudri kinare ghoomne gayi thi. Chacha ek chemical plant mein senior engineer the. Kinare par chhote-chhote chaukor khet (shallow salt pans) bane the jinmein dhoop se samudra ka paani sookh kar safed namak ke dher ban raha tha.\n\nMr. Borgaonkar ne ek mutthi safed namak uthakar kaha, \"Ketaki, jo namak (NaCl) rasoi mein 20 rupaye kilo milta hai, wahi desh ki sabse badi chemical factories ka 'King Raw Material' hai! Tumhare nahane ke sabun se lekar paani saaf karne wale bleaching powder aur cake phulane wale baking soda tak — sab isi namak ki aulaad hain.\"\n\nShaam ko jab we ghar laute, to Ketaki ki maa rasoi mein garma-garam pakode aur vanilla cake bana rahi thin. Ketaki ne dekha ki maa ne cake ke ghol mein **Baking Powder** daala jisse cake ekdam naram aur jaledar (spongy) phoola. Ketaki ko yaad aaya ki pichhle mahine jab usne galti se cake mein sirf **Baking Soda** zyada daal diya tha, to cake swaad mein **kadwa (bitter)** aur peela ho gaya tha!\n\nKetaki ne turant poocha, \"Chacha ji, samudra ke namak se ye baking soda kaise banta hai? Aur baking soda aur baking powder mein aisa kya farq hai ki ek se cake kadwa ho jaata hai aur doosre se bilkul swadisht?\"\n\nMr. Borgaonkar muskuraye: \"Bahut badhiya sawaal! Chalo, namak ki tijori se nikalne wale in ratnon ko ek-ek karke samajhte hain.\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Garmiyon ki chhuttiyon mein **Ketaki** apne chacha **Mr. Borgaonkar** ke saath Alibaug ke samudri kinare ghoomne gayi thi. Chacha ek chemical plant mein senior engineer the. Kinare par chhote-chhote chaukor khet (shallow salt pans) bane the jinmein dhoop se samudra ka paani sookh kar safed namak ke dher ban raha tha.\n\nMr. Borgaonkar ne ek mutthi safed namak uthakar kaha, \"Ketaki, jo namak (NaCl) rasoi mein 20 rupaye kilo milta hai, wahi desh ki sabse badi chemical factories ka 'King Raw Material' hai! Tumhare nahane ke sabun se lekar paani saaf karne wale bleaching powder aur cake phulane wale baking soda tak — sab isi namak ki aulaad hain.\"\n\nShaam ko jab we ghar laute, to Ketaki ki maa rasoi mein garma-garam pakode aur vanilla cake bana rahi thin. Ketaki ne dekha ki maa ne cake ke ghol mein **Baking Powder** daala jisse cake ekdam naram aur jaledar (spongy) phoola. Ketaki ko yaad aaya ki pichhle mahine jab usne galti se cake mein sirf **Baking Soda** zyada daal diya tha, to cake swaad mein **kadwa (bitter)** aur peela ho gaya tha!\n\nKetaki ne turant poocha, \"Chacha ji, samudra ke namak se ye baking soda kaise banta hai? Aur baking soda aur baking powder mein aisa kya farq hai ki ek se cake kadwa ho jaata hai aur doosre se bilkul swadisht?\"\n\nMr. Borgaonkar muskuraye: \"Bahut badhiya sawaal! Chalo, namak ki tijori se nikalne wale in ratnon ko ek-ek karke samajhte hain.\""
