            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "1. **Galti 1: Chlor-alkali process mein Anode aur Cathode ke gases ko ulta likh dena.**\n   Yaad rakho: Chloride ion (Cl⁻) negative hai, isliye wo positive electrode **Anode (+)** par jaakar **Cl₂ gas** deta hai! Aur **H₂ gas** negative electrode **Cathode (–)** par nikalti hai.\n2. **Galti 2: Bleaching powder (CaOCl₂) aur Calcium chloride (CaCl₂) ko ek samajhna.**\n   Bleaching powder **Calcium oxychloride (CaOCl₂)** hai jo dry Ca(OH)₂ + Cl₂ se banta hai; CaCl₂ mein koi bleaching gunn nahi hota!\n3. **Galti 3: Baking Soda (NaHCO₃) aur Baking Powder ko ek hi cheez maan lena.**\n   **Baking soda** sirf NaHCO₃ hai, jabki **Baking powder** = NaHCO₃ + Mild edible acid (Tartaric acid) ka mishran hai taaki Na₂CO₃ ka kadwapan khatam ho sake.\n4. **Galti 4: Baking soda ko garam karne par NaOH bana dena.**\n   NaHCO₃ ko garam karne par **Na₂CO₃ (Sodium carbonate)**, H₂O aur CO₂ banta hai (2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂), NaOH nahi!\n5. **Galti 5: \"Brine\" ka matlab pighla hua (molten) NaCl likh dena.**\n   **Brine** paani mein NaCl ka gaadha ghol (**concentrated aqueous solution of NaCl**) hota hai. Pighle hue (molten) NaCl ke electrolysis mein paani nahi hota, isliye wahan NaOH aur H₂ nahi bante (sirf Na metal aur Cl₂ banta hai)!",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. **Galti 1: Chlor-alkali process mein Anode aur Cathode ke gases ko ulta likh dena.**\n   Yaad rakho: Chloride ion (Cl⁻) negative hai, isliye wo positive electrode **Anode (+)** par jaakar **Cl₂ gas** deta hai! Aur **H₂ gas** negative electrode **Cathode (–)** par nikalti hai.\n2. **Galti 2: Bleaching powder (CaOCl₂) aur Calcium chloride (CaCl₂) ko ek samajhna.**\n   Bleaching powder **Calcium oxychloride (CaOCl₂)** hai jo dry Ca(OH)₂ + Cl₂ se banta hai; CaCl₂ mein koi bleaching gunn nahi hota!\n3. **Galti 3: Baking Soda (NaHCO₃) aur Baking Powder ko ek hi cheez maan lena.**\n   **Baking soda** sirf NaHCO₃ hai, jabki **Baking powder** = NaHCO₃ + Mild edible acid (Tartaric acid) ka mishran hai taaki Na₂CO₃ ka kadwapan khatam ho sake.\n4. **Galti 4: Baking soda ko garam karne par NaOH bana dena.**\n   NaHCO₃ ko garam karne par **Na₂CO₃ (Sodium carbonate)**, H₂O aur CO₂ banta hai (2NaHCO₃ → Na₂CO₃ + H₂O + CO₂), NaOH nahi!\n5. **Galti 5: \"Brine\" ka matlab pighla hua (molten) NaCl likh dena.**\n   **Brine** paani mein NaCl ka gaadha ghol (**concentrated aqueous solution of NaCl**) hota hai. Pighle hue (molten) NaCl ke electrolysis mein paani nahi hota, isliye wahan NaOH aur H₂ nahi bante (sirf Na metal aur Cl₂ banta hai)!"
