            "headingHinglish": "Maachis factory ki ek subah",
            "body": "Mr. Inamdar ki ek maachis (matchbox) factory mein jaan-pehchan thi, aur ek chhutti wale din wo apni bhanji Janhavi ko wahan dikhane le gaye. Gate par ek board tha: \"Andar sirf guide ke saath jaayein; kuch bhi na chhuen.\" Janhavi ne dekha ki ek lambi belt par hazaaron lakdi ki teeliyan ek ke baad ek aa rahi hain, aur unke sire par ek rangeen \"sir\" lag raha hai.\n\nGuide ne ek khaali dibbi uthakar dikhayi. \"Is dibbi ki side mein ek **bhoori-laal patti** hai, ye striker kehlati hai. Teeli ka sir akele kisi bhi sateh par nahi jalta. Sir aur patti **dono** milen, tabhi aag lagti hai.\" Janhavi ne poochha, \"Par ek hi chiz mein dono kyun nahi daal dete?\" Guide muskuraye, \"Isi sawaal ke jawab mein poora rasayan shaastra chhupa hai: patti mein ek adhaatu (phosphorus) hai, sir mein doosra adhaatu (sulphur) aur ek oxygen dene wala padarth hai, aur teeno ka alag-alag kaam hai.\"\n\nMr. Inamdar ne dheere se kaha, \"Aaj hum maachis ke bahaane **adhaatuon** ko samjhenge: ye oxygen ke saath kya karte hain, hydrogen ke saath kya, dhatuon ke saath kya, aur ek doosre ke saath kya. Aur ye sab sirf padhne ke liye: factory mein bhi bachchon ko kuch chhoone nahi diya jaata, aur ghar par maachis sirf bade jalate hain.\"",
