            "headingHinglish": "Museum ki gallery mein \"boring\" patthar",
            "body": "Mr. Pethe apne bhanje Devansh ko shahar ke museum ki **mineral gallery** mein le gaye, kyunki Devansh ke school ne agle hafte yahan ki trip rakhi thi. \"Mama, yahan to bas patthar hi patthar hain!\" Devansh ne munh bana kar kaha. Kaanch ke dibbon mein dhool-jaise bhure, kaale aur laal-bhure tukde rakhe the, aur har ek ke neeche ek chhoti si patti: *Haematite*, *Magnetite*, *Bauxite*, *Galena*, *Zinc blende*, *Malachite*.\n\nMr. Pethe muskuraye. \"Ye patthar tumhari cycle ki frame, ghar ke bartan aur wiring ka **pehla roop** hain. Ye **Haematite** dekho: laal-bhura sa, bilkul bekaar. Isse hi duniya ka bahut saara loha nikalta hai. Ye **Bauxite**: laal mitti jaisa tukda, aur isi se aluminium ka foil banta hai. Ye hara **Malachite**: isme taamba hai.\"\n\n\"Par Mama, loha to chamakta hai, ye to bilkul nahi chamak raha!\"\n\n\"Wahi to baat hai. Zameen ke andar dhatu aksar **chamakti hui dhatu ke roop mein nahi**, kisi **yaugik (compound)** ke roop mein milti hai, jaise loha, oxygen ke saath mila hua.\" Phir wo gallery ke ek kone mein gaye jahan ek chhota sa dibba alag chamak raha tha: peele rang ka ek tukda. \"Ye **sona** hai, seedha dharti se nikla hua, bina kisi mehnat ke saaf. Baaki sab patthar dull dikhte hain, par ye chamakta hai.\"\n\n\"To sona alag kyun hai?\" Devansh ki aankhein chamak uthin. \"Kyunki sone ko dharti ke andar kisi se milne ki jaldi nahi thi,\" Mr. Pethe ne hans kar kaha. \"Is baat ka jawab seedhi (reactivity series) mein chhupa hai. Chalo, ek-ek patthar ka raaz kholte hain.\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Mr. Pethe apne bhanje Devansh ko shahar ke museum ki **mineral gallery** mein le gaye, kyunki Devansh ke school ne agle hafte yahan ki trip rakhi thi. \"Mama, yahan to bas patthar hi patthar hain!\" Devansh ne munh bana kar kaha. Kaanch ke dibbon mein dhool-jaise bhure, kaale aur laal-bhure tukde rakhe the, aur har ek ke neeche ek chhoti si patti: *Haematite*, *Magnetite*, *Bauxite*, *Galena*, *Zinc blende*, *Malachite*.\n\nMr. Pethe muskuraye. \"Ye patthar tumhari cycle ki frame, ghar ke bartan aur wiring ka **pehla roop** hain. Ye **Haematite** dekho: laal-bhura sa, bilkul bekaar. Isse hi duniya ka bahut saara loha nikalta hai. Ye **Bauxite**: laal mitti jaisa tukda, aur isi se aluminium ka foil banta hai. Ye hara **Malachite**: isme taamba hai.\"\n\n\"Par Mama, loha to chamakta hai, ye to bilkul nahi chamak raha!\"\n\n\"Wahi to baat hai. Zameen ke andar dhatu aksar **chamakti hui dhatu ke roop mein nahi**, kisi **yaugik (compound)** ke roop mein milti hai, jaise loha, oxygen ke saath mila hua.\" Phir wo gallery ke ek kone mein gaye jahan ek chhota sa dibba alag chamak raha tha: peele rang ka ek tukda. \"Ye **sona** hai, seedha dharti se nikla hua, bina kisi mehnat ke saaf. Baaki sab patthar dull dikhte hain, par ye chamakta hai.\"\n\n\"To sona alag kyun hai?\" Devansh ki aankhein chamak uthin. \"Kyunki sone ko dharti ke andar kisi se milne ki jaldi nahi thi,\" Mr. Pethe ne hans kar kaha. \"Is baat ka jawab seedhi (reactivity series) mein chhupa hai. Chalo, ek-ek patthar ka raaz kholte hain.\""
