            "body": "Mr. Tendulkar ki bhatiji Anagha ko school-fete (mela) mein ek stall milega, aur stall ke liye **40 cakes** ka order hai. Mr. Tendulkar ne purani recipe-card nikaali: **1 cake ke liye 2 ande, 200 g maida, 100 g cheeni, 50 g butter.** Anagha ne turant likha: \"Chacha, 40 cake matlab sab kuch **40 guna**: 80 ande, 8000 g yaani 8 kg maida, 4 kg cheeni, 2 kg butter.\" Mr. Tendulkar muskuraye: \"Bilkul. Recipe ek **ratio** hai. Cake kitne banane hain, bas wahi **guna karne wali sankhya** (scale factor) hai.\"\n\nPhir unhone ek doosra card dikhaya, jo unki nani ke zamane ka tha: **\"2 ande, 1 katori maida, 1 katori cheeni.\"** Anagha ne kaha: \"Is mein maida aur cheeni ka ratio 1 : 1 hai, to dono ka **vazan** bhi barabar hoga.\" Mr. Tendulkar ne rasoi ki taraazu par ek **barabar katori** maida aur ek **barabar katori** cheeni tole. Maida lagbhag **100 g** nikla, cheeni lagbhag **150 g**. \"Dekha? **Ginti** (katori) mein ratio 1 : 1 hai, par **vazan** mein ratio 100 : 150, yaani 2 : 3 hai. Kyunki cheeni ki ek katori maida ki katori se bhaari hoti hai.\"\n\nAnagha ne aankhein badi kar ke kaha: \"Chacha, ye to bilkul chemistry jaisa hai! Equation ke aage ke numbers bhi **'katori'** (ginti) hote honge, vazan nahi!\" Mr. Tendulkar ne taali baja di: \"Yahi aaj ka poora topic hai. Equation ek **recipe** hai, aur uski 'katori' ka naam **mole** hai.\"\n\n**Ghar par kar sakte ho (bade ke saath, 5 minute):** ek hi katori se chawal, atta aur cheeni tolo (har baar katori barabar bhari, upar se saaf). Ginti barabar, par vazan alag-alag aayega. Taraazu na ho to haath mein uthakar mehsoos karo: cheeni aur chawal bhaari lagenge, atta halka.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Mr. Tendulkar ki bhatiji Anagha ko school-fete (mela) mein ek stall milega, aur stall ke liye **40 cakes** ka order hai. Mr. Tendulkar ne purani recipe-card nikaali: **1 cake ke liye 2 ande, 200 g maida, 100 g cheeni, 50 g butter.** Anagha ne turant likha: \"Chacha, 40 cake matlab sab kuch **40 guna**: 80 ande, 8000 g yaani 8 kg maida, 4 kg cheeni, 2 kg butter.\" Mr. Tendulkar muskuraye: \"Bilkul. Recipe ek **ratio** hai. Cake kitne banane hain, bas wahi **guna karne wali sankhya** (scale factor) hai.\"\n\nPhir unhone ek doosra card dikhaya, jo unki nani ke zamane ka tha: **\"2 ande, 1 katori maida, 1 katori cheeni.\"** Anagha ne kaha: \"Is mein maida aur cheeni ka ratio 1 : 1 hai, to dono ka **vazan** bhi barabar hoga.\" Mr. Tendulkar ne rasoi ki taraazu par ek **barabar katori** maida aur ek **barabar katori** cheeni tole. Maida lagbhag **100 g** nikla, cheeni lagbhag **150 g**. \"Dekha? **Ginti** (katori) mein ratio 1 : 1 hai, par **vazan** mein ratio 100 : 150, yaani 2 : 3 hai. Kyunki cheeni ki ek katori maida ki katori se bhaari hoti hai.\"\n\nAnagha ne aankhein badi kar ke kaha: \"Chacha, ye to bilkul chemistry jaisa hai! Equation ke aage ke numbers bhi **'katori'** (ginti) hote honge, vazan nahi!\" Mr. Tendulkar ne taali baja di: \"Yahi aaj ka poora topic hai. Equation ek **recipe** hai, aur uski 'katori' ka naam **mole** hai.\"\n\n**Ghar par kar sakte ho (bade ke saath, 5 minute):** ek hi katori se chawal, atta aur cheeni tolo (har baar katori barabar bhari, upar se saaf). Ginti barabar, par vazan alag-alag aayega. Taraazu na ho to haath mein uthakar mehsoos karo: cheeni aur chawal bhaari lagenge, atta halka."
