            "correctIndex": 3,
            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"22.4 L har cheez ka ek mole hota hai, liquid aur thos ka bhi.\"): Naiysha ki ek dost ne kaha: \"36 g paani ka volume 2 × 22.4 = 44.8 L hoga.\" Par 36 g paani 2 mol hai, aur liquid paani ka volume lagbhag 36 mL hota hai (1 g paani = lagbhag 1 mL). Yaani 44.8 L se lagbhag 1200 guna chhota: ek chhoti katori mein samaa jaata hai. Wajah: liquid mein kan paas-paas hote hain, gas mein bahut door-door; 22.4 L sirf gas ke liye hai. Bhaap ke liye bhi 22.4 L nahi: 273 K par paani gas hi nahi hota, aur 100 °C (373 K) par 1 mol bhaap 1 atm par 22.4 × 373 ÷ 273 = lagbhag 30.6 L leti hai (Class 9 ka Charles ka niyam). Thos ke saath bhi wahi: CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂ mein sirf CO₂ ka volume gas ke roop mein ginte, CaO thos hai, uska volume litre mein nahi.",
