            "heading": "Part B: Atomic radius kaise naapte hain (ek chhoti si baat)",
            "headingHinglish": "Part B: Atomic radius kaise naapte hain (ek chhoti si baat)",
            "body": "Atom ki koi seedhi \"deewar\" nahi hoti, isliye uska radius hum ek tareeke se **tay** karte hain: jaise do ek jaise atoms jab chipak kar baithe hon (dhatu ke jaal mein ya bond mein), to unke nucleus ke beech ki doori ka aadha. Isliye tables mein sankhyaein thodi alag-alag milti hain, jo is baat par nirbhar karti hain ki kis tareeke se naapa gaya. **Trend (order) har table mein wahi rehta hai**, isliye hum kuch mashhoor, lagbhag values ka ek hi set use karenge. Ye values 1 pm = 10⁻¹² m mein hain.\n\n**Noble gases ke baare mein ek line:** He, Ne, Ar jaise atoms kisi se bond hi nahi banate, isliye unka size doosre tareeke se naapte hain aur wo values dusre atoms se seedhi milti nahi. Isliye is topic mein trend Li se F aur Na se Cl tak dekhte hain (jaise Class 9 mein bhi kiya tha).",
            "bodyHinglish": "Atom ki koi seedhi \"deewar\" nahi hoti, isliye uska radius hum ek tareeke se **tay** karte hain: jaise do ek jaise atoms jab chipak kar baithe hon (dhatu ke jaal mein ya bond mein), to unke nucleus ke beech ki doori ka aadha. Isliye tables mein sankhyaein thodi alag-alag milti hain, jo is baat par nirbhar karti hain ki kis tareeke se naapa gaya. **Trend (order) har table mein wahi rehta hai**, isliye hum kuch mashhoor, lagbhag values ka ek hi set use karenge. Ye values 1 pm = 10⁻¹² m mein hain.\n\n**Noble gases ke baare mein ek line:** He, Ne, Ar jaise atoms kisi se bond hi nahi banate, isliye unka size doosre tareeke se naapte hain aur wo values dusre atoms se seedhi milti nahi. Isliye is topic mein trend Li se F aur Na se Cl tak dekhte hain (jaise Class 9 mein bhi kiya tha)."
