            "body": "Sardi ki raat thi. Mr. Vaidya apne bhatije Swanand ke saath ek rishtedaar ke ghar gaye the. Drawing room mein sofa par padosi ke do chhote bachche ek hi kambal mein dubke baithe the, aur tivi par kuch dekh rahe the. Swanand ne dekha ki kambal ek taraf **khisakta ja raha tha**: ek bachcha apni taraf zor se kheench raha tha, doosre ka kandha khula reh gaya aur wo thithurne laga.\n\nSwanand ne dheere se kaha, \"Chacha, kambal to dono ka hai, phir ek ke paas zyada kyun?\" Mr. Vaidya muskuraye. \"Kyunki dono ki **kheenchne ki taakat** barabar nahi hai. Agar dono barabar kheenchte, to kambal theek beech mein rehta aur dono ko aadha-aadha milta. Ek zyada zor lagaata hai, to kambal uski taraf khisakta hai. Aur agar ek itna zor lagaye ki **poora kambal** apni taraf kar le, to doosre ke paas kuch bacha hi nahi.\"\n\nSwanand ki aankhein chamak gayi. \"Chacha, ye to bond jaisa hai na? Do atom, aur beech mein shared electrons ka kambal!\" Mr. Vaidya ne shabaashi di. \"Bilkul. Har atom ki ek **kheenchne ki aadat** hoti hai. Use hi chemistry mein **electronegativity** kehte hain. Chalo, dekhte hain ki kis atom ki aadat kitni zor ki hai, aur wo table mein kahan kaise badalti hai.\"\n\n```\n   1) Dono barabar kheenchte hain       A  ----[ kambal ]----  B    kambal beech mein\n   2) B thoda zyada kheenchta hai       A  ------[ kambal ]--  B    kambal B ki taraf khisak gaya\n   3) B poora kheench leta hai          A         [ kambal ]-  B    kambal poora B ke paas\n```\n\n> **Figure 4.1** – Kambal ki tarah shared electrons: A aur B ki kheench ka farq jitna bada, kambal utna hi ek taraf. Yahi baat bond mein electrons ke jode (shared pair) ke saath hoti hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Sardi ki raat thi. Mr. Vaidya apne bhatije Swanand ke saath ek rishtedaar ke ghar gaye the. Drawing room mein sofa par padosi ke do chhote bachche ek hi kambal mein dubke baithe the, aur tivi par kuch dekh rahe the. Swanand ne dekha ki kambal ek taraf **khisakta ja raha tha**: ek bachcha apni taraf zor se kheench raha tha, doosre ka kandha khula reh gaya aur wo thithurne laga.\n\nSwanand ne dheere se kaha, \"Chacha, kambal to dono ka hai, phir ek ke paas zyada kyun?\" Mr. Vaidya muskuraye. \"Kyunki dono ki **kheenchne ki taakat** barabar nahi hai. Agar dono barabar kheenchte, to kambal theek beech mein rehta aur dono ko aadha-aadha milta. Ek zyada zor lagaata hai, to kambal uski taraf khisakta hai. Aur agar ek itna zor lagaye ki **poora kambal** apni taraf kar le, to doosre ke paas kuch bacha hi nahi.\"\n\nSwanand ki aankhein chamak gayi. \"Chacha, ye to bond jaisa hai na? Do atom, aur beech mein shared electrons ka kambal!\" Mr. Vaidya ne shabaashi di. \"Bilkul. Har atom ki ek **kheenchne ki aadat** hoti hai. Use hi chemistry mein **electronegativity** kehte hain. Chalo, dekhte hain ki kis atom ki aadat kitni zor ki hai, aur wo table mein kahan kaise badalti hai.\"\n\n```\n   1) Dono barabar kheenchte hain       A  ----[ kambal ]----  B    kambal beech mein\n   2) B thoda zyada kheenchta hai       A  ------[ kambal ]--  B    kambal B ki taraf khisak gaya\n   3) B poora kheench leta hai          A         [ kambal ]-  B    kambal poora B ke paas\n```\n\n> **Figure 4.1** – Kambal ki tarah shared electrons: A aur B ki kheench ka farq jitna bada, kambal utna hi ek taraf. Yahi baat bond mein electrons ke jode (shared pair) ke saath hoti hai."
