            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"Sabse zyada electronegative tatva sabse reactive metal hota hai.\"): Dekho: sabse zyada electronegative F hai, aur wo ek non-metal hai (halogen). Sabse kam electronegative tatva Cs aur Fr hain, aur ve bahut reactive metals hain (Group 1). Matlab \"bahut kheenchne wala\" aur \"reactive metal\" ek hi cheez nahi hai: reactive metal wo hai jo electron dene mein khush hai, aur uski kheench kam hoti hai. Demo: F (4.0) ko \"sabse bada kheenchne wala\" maan lo, to wo electron lene wala non-metal hai, dene wala nahi. Ab K (0.8) ko dekho: bahut kam kheench, isliye wo apna baahari electron aasani se de deta hai (Topic 2), aur isi wajah se Group 1 ke metals tez react karte hain (sirf padhne ke liye). Matlab: bada number = lene wala, chhota number = dene wala, aur \"reactive metal\" chhote number wala hota hai.",
