            "body": "Mr. Yewale ki bhanji Kaveri chhuttiyon mein unke yahan aayi thi. Mohalle ki ek chhoti lending library mein Mr. Yewale ka khaata tha, aur Kaveri ko wo wahan le gaye. Library ke bahar ek board laga tha: \"Dene wale sadasya\" aur \"Lene wale sadasya\".\n\nKaveri ne dekha ki kuch sadasya hamesha kitaab **dene** ke liye taiyaar rehte the: bas koi maange, to haath badha kar de dete. Doosre sadasya hamesha kitaab **lene** ke chakkar mein rehte, aur ek baar le lene ke baad kabhi waapas nahi dete. Aur kuch beech wale the, jo kabhi dete, kabhi lete.\n\n\"Mama, ye sab alag-alag kyun hain?\" Kaveri ne poochha. \"Ek hi library mein sab ek jaise kyun nahi?\"\n\nMr. Yewale muskuraye. \"Dekho, jinki kitaab unse door, ooperi manzil par rakhi hai aur jinki pakad dheeli hai, wo dene mein aasaan hain. Aur jinka sanduk bas **ek ya do kitaab se adhoora** hai aur jo use poora karna chahte hain, wo lene mein utsuk hain. Tatvon mein bhi bilkul yahi hota hai. **Electron wo kitaab hai.** Kuch atom use dene mein khush rehte hain, kuch lene mein.\"\n\n```\n   Library ka board\n\n   DENE WALE (lender)                     LENE WALE (borrower)\n   kitaab door aur halki pakad            kitaab ki kami, pakad majboot\n\n   Na  Mg  Al   <----  beech ke  ---->   P   S   Cl\n   (dhatu)            sadasya (Si)     (adhaatu)\n\n   dete hain  ----------------------->  lete hain\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.1** – Period 3 ko library ka board maano: baayen taraf ke tatva electron (kitaab) **dene** mein aasaan, daayen taraf ke **lene** mein aasaan, aur beech mein Si jaise tatva donon ke beech jhoolte hain.\n\nWapas ghar jaate hue Kaveri ne ek line apni copy mein likhi: \"Dhatu = dene wala. Adhaatu = lene wala.\" Mr. Yewale ne kaha: \"Bilkul sahi. Ab isi line ko poori table tak failate hain.\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Mr. Yewale ki bhanji Kaveri chhuttiyon mein unke yahan aayi thi. Mohalle ki ek chhoti lending library mein Mr. Yewale ka khaata tha, aur Kaveri ko wo wahan le gaye. Library ke bahar ek board laga tha: \"Dene wale sadasya\" aur \"Lene wale sadasya\".\n\nKaveri ne dekha ki kuch sadasya hamesha kitaab **dene** ke liye taiyaar rehte the: bas koi maange, to haath badha kar de dete. Doosre sadasya hamesha kitaab **lene** ke chakkar mein rehte, aur ek baar le lene ke baad kabhi waapas nahi dete. Aur kuch beech wale the, jo kabhi dete, kabhi lete.\n\n\"Mama, ye sab alag-alag kyun hain?\" Kaveri ne poochha. \"Ek hi library mein sab ek jaise kyun nahi?\"\n\nMr. Yewale muskuraye. \"Dekho, jinki kitaab unse door, ooperi manzil par rakhi hai aur jinki pakad dheeli hai, wo dene mein aasaan hain. Aur jinka sanduk bas **ek ya do kitaab se adhoora** hai aur jo use poora karna chahte hain, wo lene mein utsuk hain. Tatvon mein bhi bilkul yahi hota hai. **Electron wo kitaab hai.** Kuch atom use dene mein khush rehte hain, kuch lene mein.\"\n\n```\n   Library ka board\n\n   DENE WALE (lender)                     LENE WALE (borrower)\n   kitaab door aur halki pakad            kitaab ki kami, pakad majboot\n\n   Na  Mg  Al   <----  beech ke  ---->   P   S   Cl\n   (dhatu)            sadasya (Si)     (adhaatu)\n\n   dete hain  ----------------------->  lete hain\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.1** – Period 3 ko library ka board maano: baayen taraf ke tatva electron (kitaab) **dene** mein aasaan, daayen taraf ke **lene** mein aasaan, aur beech mein Si jaise tatva donon ke beech jhoolte hain.\n\nWapas ghar jaate hue Kaveri ne ek line apni copy mein likhi: \"Dhatu = dene wala. Adhaatu = lene wala.\" Mr. Yewale ne kaha: \"Bilkul sahi. Ab isi line ko poori table tak failate hain.\""
