          {
            "heading": "Part D: Sab ek saath: position dekh kar sab kuch bata do",
            "headingHinglish": "Part D: Sab ek saath: position dekh kar sab kuch bata do",
            "body": "Ab tak hum alag-alag properties dekh rahe the. Ek poora \"trend map\" banate hain jismein chhah properties ek saath hain (sab ke liye lagbhag, general trend; chhote apwaad aage ki class mein):\n\n```\n   Ek PERIOD mein baayen se daayen  ------------->\n\n   Atomic size:            ghatta hai\n   Ionisation energy:      badhti hai\n   Electron affinity:      badhti hai\n   Electronegativity:      badhti hai\n   Metallic character:     ghatta hai\n   Non-metallic character: badhta hai\n\n   Ek GROUP mein upar se neeche (v)\n\n   Atomic size:            badhta hai\n   Ionisation energy:      ghatti hai\n   Electron affinity:      ghatti hai\n   Electronegativity:      ghatti hai\n   Metallic character:     badhta hai\n   Non-metallic character: ghatta hai\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.5** – Trend map: ek period mein baayen se daayen aur ek group mein upar se neeche chhah properties kaise badalti hain. Dhyan do: jahan size ghatta hai wahan ionisation energy, electron affinity aur electronegativity badhti hain; dono \"chhote atom\" ke saath chalte hain.\n\nChhoti si yaadgaar: **size, metallic character aur dhatu ki reactivity ek taraf chalte hain; IE, EA, EN aur non-metallic character doosri taraf.**\n\n### Example 8. Anjaan tatva X: configuration 2, 8, 3\n\nIs tatva ki sab kuch bataiye: group, period, dhatu ya adhaatu, valency, banne wala ion, uska size aur oxide ki prakriti.\n\n- Electrons = 2 + 8 + 3 = 13, to Z = 13: **aluminium (Al)**.\n- 3 shells, to **Period 3**. 3 valence electrons, to **Group 13** (3 + 10).\n- Baayen taraf aur beech ka: **dhatu** (seedhi ke baayen).\n- Valency 3 (3 electron dene hain).\n- Ion: **Al³⁺** (3 electron nikal jaate hain). Naya configuration 2, 8 (neon jaisa), 10 electrons.\n- Size: **Al³⁺, Al atom se chhota** (3 electron gaye, ek poori shell kam, aur 13 protons ab sirf 10 electron ko kheench rahe hain). Al ka radius lagbhag 143 pm.\n- Oxide: **Al₂O₃**, amphoteric.\n\n**Jaanch:** Al₂O₃ mein 2 × (+3) = +6 aur 3 × (−2) = −6, total 0 ✅. Al ka valency 3 aur Group 13: 13 − 10 = 3 ✅.\n\n### Example 9. Anjaan tatva Y: clues se pehchano\n\n**Sawaal:** Tatva Y Period 3 mein hai, wo anion Y⁻ banata hai jiske 18 electron hain, aur uska oxide bahut tez acidic hai. Y kaun hai, aur kaisa hai?\n\n- Y⁻ mein 18 electron, to Y ke 17 electron: Z = 17, **chlorine (Cl)**, configuration 2, 8, 7.\n- 7 valence electrons: **Group 17**, valency 1. **Adhaatu**, halogen.\n- Ion **Cl⁻** (ek electron liya), bada hai Cl se (electron zyada, protons wahi 17).\n- Oxide **Cl₂O₇**, bahut acidic, paani mein HClO₄.\n- Non-metallic character Period 3 mein sabse zyada (noble gas ko chhodkar), aur reactivity bhi Period 3 ke non-metals mein sabse zyada.\n\n**Jaanch:** Cl₂O₇ + H₂O → 2HClO₄: Cl 2, O 8, H 2 dono taraf ✅. Cl⁻ ka configuration 2, 8, 8 (argon jaisa), 18 electron ✅.\n\n### Example 10. B, Al aur Ga: ek hi group, alag swabhav\n\n**Sawaal:** B, Al aur Ga Group 13 mein hain, upar se neeche. Dhatu-pan ka order aur kaaran batao.\n\n- B (2 shell), Al (3 shell), Ga (4 shell, sirf naam).\n- Neeche utarte hue baahari electron door aur dheela, to **metallic character badhta hai**: B < Al < Ga.\n- B metalloid hai, Al dhatu, Ga dhatu.\n\n**Jaanch:** Group mein neeche metallic character badhta hai ✅ aur B seedhi par baitha hai ✅.\n\n### Example 11. Br₂ aur KI ka milna\n\n**Sawaal:** Br₂ (laal-bhoora liquid, sirf dekhne ke liye) KI ke ghol mein mile to kya hoga? Likho.\n\n- Br₂, I₂ se upar hai (Figure 5.3), to Br₂ I₂ ko nikaal dega.\n- Br₂ + 2KI → 2KBr + I₂.\n\n**Jaanch:** baayen Br 2, K 2, I 2; daayen K 2, Br 2, I 2 ✅.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ab tak hum alag-alag properties dekh rahe the. Ek poora \"trend map\" banate hain jismein chhah properties ek saath hain (sab ke liye lagbhag, general trend; chhote apwaad aage ki class mein):\n\n```\n   Ek PERIOD mein baayen se daayen  ------------->\n\n   Atomic size:            ghatta hai\n   Ionisation energy:      badhti hai\n   Electron affinity:      badhti hai\n   Electronegativity:      badhti hai\n   Metallic character:     ghatta hai\n   Non-metallic character: badhta hai\n\n   Ek GROUP mein upar se neeche (v)\n\n   Atomic size:            badhta hai\n   Ionisation energy:      ghatti hai\n   Electron affinity:      ghatti hai\n   Electronegativity:      ghatti hai\n   Metallic character:     badhta hai\n   Non-metallic character: ghatta hai\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.5** – Trend map: ek period mein baayen se daayen aur ek group mein upar se neeche chhah properties kaise badalti hain. Dhyan do: jahan size ghatta hai wahan ionisation energy, electron affinity aur electronegativity badhti hain; dono \"chhote atom\" ke saath chalte hain.\n\nChhoti si yaadgaar: **size, metallic character aur dhatu ki reactivity ek taraf chalte hain; IE, EA, EN aur non-metallic character doosri taraf.**\n\n### Example 8. Anjaan tatva X: configuration 2, 8, 3\n\nIs tatva ki sab kuch bataiye: group, period, dhatu ya adhaatu, valency, banne wala ion, uska size aur oxide ki prakriti.\n\n- Electrons = 2 + 8 + 3 = 13, to Z = 13: **aluminium (Al)**.\n- 3 shells, to **Period 3**. 3 valence electrons, to **Group 13** (3 + 10).\n- Baayen taraf aur beech ka: **dhatu** (seedhi ke baayen).\n- Valency 3 (3 electron dene hain).\n- Ion: **Al³⁺** (3 electron nikal jaate hain). Naya configuration 2, 8 (neon jaisa), 10 electrons.\n- Size: **Al³⁺, Al atom se chhota** (3 electron gaye, ek poori shell kam, aur 13 protons ab sirf 10 electron ko kheench rahe hain). Al ka radius lagbhag 143 pm.\n- Oxide: **Al₂O₃**, amphoteric.\n\n**Jaanch:** Al₂O₃ mein 2 × (+3) = +6 aur 3 × (−2) = −6, total 0 ✅. Al ka valency 3 aur Group 13: 13 − 10 = 3 ✅.\n\n### Example 9. Anjaan tatva Y: clues se pehchano\n\n**Sawaal:** Tatva Y Period 3 mein hai, wo anion Y⁻ banata hai jiske 18 electron hain, aur uska oxide bahut tez acidic hai. Y kaun hai, aur kaisa hai?\n\n- Y⁻ mein 18 electron, to Y ke 17 electron: Z = 17, **chlorine (Cl)**, configuration 2, 8, 7.\n- 7 valence electrons: **Group 17**, valency 1. **Adhaatu**, halogen.\n- Ion **Cl⁻** (ek electron liya), bada hai Cl se (electron zyada, protons wahi 17).\n- Oxide **Cl₂O₇**, bahut acidic, paani mein HClO₄.\n- Non-metallic character Period 3 mein sabse zyada (noble gas ko chhodkar), aur reactivity bhi Period 3 ke non-metals mein sabse zyada.\n\n**Jaanch:** Cl₂O₇ + H₂O → 2HClO₄: Cl 2, O 8, H 2 dono taraf ✅. Cl⁻ ka configuration 2, 8, 8 (argon jaisa), 18 electron ✅.\n\n### Example 10. B, Al aur Ga: ek hi group, alag swabhav\n\n**Sawaal:** B, Al aur Ga Group 13 mein hain, upar se neeche. Dhatu-pan ka order aur kaaran batao.\n\n- B (2 shell), Al (3 shell), Ga (4 shell, sirf naam).\n- Neeche utarte hue baahari electron door aur dheela, to **metallic character badhta hai**: B < Al < Ga.\n- B metalloid hai, Al dhatu, Ga dhatu.\n\n**Jaanch:** Group mein neeche metallic character badhta hai ✅ aur B seedhi par baitha hai ✅.\n\n### Example 11. Br₂ aur KI ka milna\n\n**Sawaal:** Br₂ (laal-bhoora liquid, sirf dekhne ke liye) KI ke ghol mein mile to kya hoga? Likho.\n\n- Br₂, I₂ se upar hai (Figure 5.3), to Br₂ I₂ ko nikaal dega.\n- Br₂ + 2KI → 2KBr + I₂.\n\n**Jaanch:** baayen Br 2, K 2, I 2; daayen K 2, Br 2, I 2 ✅."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti: \"Neeche utarte hue dhatu aur adhaatu dono ki reactivity badhti hai.\"**\n\nYe galti isliye hoti hai ki \"reactivity\" shabd dono ke liye ek hi hai, par dono ka matlab alag hai. Dhatu ki reactivity = electron **dene** ki taiyari. Adhaatu ki reactivity = electron **lene** ki taiyari. Group mein neeche utarte hue baahari electron **door** hota hai: ye electron dene ko aasaan banata hai par lene ko mushkil.\n\n*Demonstration 1: library se.* Maano library ki ek nayi shakha khuli jahan kitaabein ooperi manzil se bhi door, teesri manzil par rakhi hain. Jo sadasya kitaab **dena** chahta hai, uske liye ab aur aasaan: kitaab uske haath se door, pakad dheeli. Par jo sadasya kitaab **lena** chahta hai, use wo kitaab ab door se kheenchni padegi: kheench kamzor, utsukta kam. Neeche utarte hue shell door hoti jaati hai: dene wala aur tatpar, lene wala aur kamzor.\n\n*Demonstration 2: asli reactions se.* Group 1: K, Na se zyada tezi se react karta hai (teacher demo; electron door, ionisation energy 419 < 496 lagbhag). Group 17: Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂ hota hai, par Br₂ + 2KCl → kuch nahi hota. Agar adhaatu ki reactivity neeche badhti, to Br₂ Cl₂ ko uske salt se nikaal deta. Par aisa nahi hota: **Cl₂ Br₂ se zyada reactive hai**. Is tarah ek hi direction (neeche) mein dhatu ki reactivity **badhti** hai aur adhaatu ki **ghatti**.\n\nJaanch: Li < Na < K (badhti) aur F > Cl > Br > I (ghatti) ✅.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti: \"Neeche utarte hue dhatu aur adhaatu dono ki reactivity badhti hai.\"**\n\nYe galti isliye hoti hai ki \"reactivity\" shabd dono ke liye ek hi hai, par dono ka matlab alag hai. Dhatu ki reactivity = electron **dene** ki taiyari. Adhaatu ki reactivity = electron **lene** ki taiyari. Group mein neeche utarte hue baahari electron **door** hota hai: ye electron dene ko aasaan banata hai par lene ko mushkil.\n\n*Demonstration 1: library se.* Maano library ki ek nayi shakha khuli jahan kitaabein ooperi manzil se bhi door, teesri manzil par rakhi hain. Jo sadasya kitaab **dena** chahta hai, uske liye ab aur aasaan: kitaab uske haath se door, pakad dheeli. Par jo sadasya kitaab **lena** chahta hai, use wo kitaab ab door se kheenchni padegi: kheench kamzor, utsukta kam. Neeche utarte hue shell door hoti jaati hai: dene wala aur tatpar, lene wala aur kamzor.\n\n*Demonstration 2: asli reactions se.* Group 1: K, Na se zyada tezi se react karta hai (teacher demo; electron door, ionisation energy 419 < 496 lagbhag). Group 17: Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂ hota hai, par Br₂ + 2KCl → kuch nahi hota. Agar adhaatu ki reactivity neeche badhti, to Br₂ Cl₂ ko uske salt se nikaal deta. Par aisa nahi hota: **Cl₂ Br₂ se zyada reactive hai**. Is tarah ek hi direction (neeche) mein dhatu ki reactivity **badhti** hai aur adhaatu ki **ghatti**.\n\nJaanch: Li < Na < K (badhti) aur F > Cl > Br > I (ghatti) ✅."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Metallic character** = electron dene ki aasani (ionisation energy kam). **Non-metallic character** = electron lene ki aasani (EA aur EN zyada).\n- Period mein baayen se daayen: metallic character **ghatta**, non-metallic **badhta**. Group mein neeche: metallic **badhta**, non-metallic **ghatta**.\n- Dhatu ki reactivity: group mein neeche **badhti**, period mein daayen **ghat-ti**. Adhaatu ki reactivity: group mein neeche **ghat-ti** (F > Cl > Br > I), period mein daayen **badhti**.\n- Halogens ki seedhi: upar wala halogen neeche wale ko uske salt se nikaalta hai (Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂); ulta nahi hota. Sirf padhne ke liye.\n- Period 3 ke oxide: Na₂O, MgO basic; Al₂O₃ amphoteric; SiO₂ kamzor acidic; P₄O₁₀, SO₃ acidic; Cl₂O₇ bahut acidic.\n- Group 1 ke hydroxide neeche utarte hue tez base: LiOH < NaOH < KOH.\n- Table mein jagah dekh kar group, period, dhatu ya adhaatu, valency, ion, size aur oxide ki prakriti sab bata sakte hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Metallic character** = electron dene ki aasani (ionisation energy kam). **Non-metallic character** = electron lene ki aasani (EA aur EN zyada).\n- Period mein baayen se daayen: metallic character **ghatta**, non-metallic **badhta**. Group mein neeche: metallic **badhta**, non-metallic **ghatta**.\n- Dhatu ki reactivity: group mein neeche **badhti**, period mein daayen **ghat-ti**. Adhaatu ki reactivity: group mein neeche **ghat-ti** (F > Cl > Br > I), period mein daayen **badhti**.\n- Halogens ki seedhi: upar wala halogen neeche wale ko uske salt se nikaalta hai (Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂); ulta nahi hota. Sirf padhne ke liye.\n- Period 3 ke oxide: Na₂O, MgO basic; Al₂O₃ amphoteric; SiO₂ kamzor acidic; P₄O₁₀, SO₃ acidic; Cl₂O₇ bahut acidic.\n- Group 1 ke hydroxide neeche utarte hue tez base: LiOH < NaOH < KOH.\n- Table mein jagah dekh kar group, period, dhatu ya adhaatu, valency, ion, size aur oxide ki prakriti sab bata sakte hain."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "(Sab sawaal paper par hal karne ke liye hain; alkali metals, halogens aur tez acid ya alkali wale sawaal sirf padhne ke liye hain.)\n\n1. Arrange K, Ca and Mg in decreasing order of metallic character. Give a reason using shells and the number of electrons.\n2. Atomic number 20 is an element. Find its configuration, group, period, valency, the ion it forms, whether the ion is bigger or smaller than the atom, and the nature of its oxide.\n3. Chlorine water (Cl₂ dissolved in water) is added to separate solutions of KCl, KBr and KI. In which solutions will a reaction take place? Write the equation(s) and explain using the halogen ladder. (Fact given: Cl₂ is more reactive than Br₂ and I₂.)\n4. Name the oxide of each element with its type: Na, Al, S, P. Which one reacts with both an acid and a base?\n5. Three metals P, Q and R are Na, Mg and Al in some order. P reacts violently with cold water (teacher demo), Q reacts very slowly with cold water but faster with hot water and steam, and R does not react with cold or hot water and reacts only with steam (its oxide layer protects it). Arrange them in decreasing order of reactivity and identify each.\n6. Why does the metallic character increase from B to Al to Ga? Why is B called a metalloid?\n7. Compare the reactivity of metals and non-metals as we go down a group. A student says both increase. Show the error with examples.\n8. Arrange LiOH, NaOH and KOH in order of increasing basic strength. Give the reason in terms of metallic character.\n9. Arrange MgO, Cl₂O₇, SiO₂ and P₄O₁₀ in increasing order of acidic nature.\n10. Which is the most non-metallic element among Cl, Br and I, and which is the most metallic among Mg, Ca and Sr (strontium, just below Ca in Group 2)? Give reasons using the number of shells.\n11. The first ionisation energy of K is about 419 kJ per mol and of Ca about 590 kJ per mol. (a) How much energy is needed to remove one electron from each atom in 5 mol of K atoms? (b) The same for 5 mol of Ca atoms. (c) Which of the two metals is more reactive from this data, and why? (Gaseous atoms, first ionisation energy only.)\n12. Why is I₂ unable to take Br⁻ out of KBr, though both are halogens? Give two reasons based on the trend.\n13. State True or False and correct the false ones: (a) Metallic character increases from Na to Cl. (b) Cl₂O₇ is the most acidic oxide in Period 3. (c) Al₂O₃ is a basic oxide. (d) Reactivity of F₂ is higher than that of Cl₂. (e) An element with configuration 2, 8, 1 is more metallic than one with 2, 8, 8, 1.\n14. An element Z has configuration 2, 3. Find its group, period, valency, and whether it is metal, non-metal or metalloid. Predict whether its oxide is acidic or basic, and whether it is more or less metallic than Al.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. K: 4 shells, 1 valence electron. Ca: 4 shells, 2 valence electrons. Mg: 3 shells, 2 valence electrons. K aur Ca ke shells barabar, par Ca mein 20 protons aur K mein 19, to Ca ka kheench zyada, K sabse aasani se electron deta hai. Mg ke 3 hi shells, to electron nucleus ke paas aur kheench zyada. **K > Ca > Mg**. Jaanch: ionisation energy lagbhag 419 < 590 < 738 ✅.\n2. Z = 20: configuration **2, 8, 8, 2**. 4 shells, to **Period 4**; 2 valence electrons, **Group 2** (2 valence electron). Valency 2. Ion **Ca²⁺** (2, 8, 8, argon jaisa, 18 electron). Ion atom se **chhota** (4th shell gayi, 20 protons 18 electron ko kheench rahe hain). Oxide **CaO**, basic (Ca dhatu hai). Jaanch: CaO mein +2 aur −2 ✅. Ye element Ca hai.\n3. Cl₂ Br₂ aur I₂ dono se zyada reactive hai. **KBr aur KI** mein reaction hoga, KCl mein nahi (Cl⁻ ko Cl₂ nikaal hi nahi sakta, wo pehle se Cl hai). Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂ (K 2, Cl 2, Br 2 dono taraf ✅). Cl₂ + 2KI → 2KCl + I₂ (K 2, Cl 2, I 2 ✅). **KCl:** koi nayi cheez nahi bani.\n4. Na: **Na₂O**, basic. Al: **Al₂O₃**, amphoteric. S: **SO₃**, acidic. P: **P₄O₁₀**, acidic. **Al₂O₃** acid aur base dono se reaction karta hai (Al₂O₃ + 6HCl → 2AlCl₃ + 3H₂O aur Al₂O₃ + 2NaOH → 2NaAlO₂ + H₂O). Jaanch: Al 2, O 3, H 6, Cl 6 dono taraf ✅.\n5. Reactivity: P > Q > R. Period 3 mein baayen se daayen reactivity ghatti hai, to **P = Na, Q = Mg, R = Al**. Jaanch: ionisation energy lagbhag Na 496 < Mg 738, aur Al ke 3 electron ko nikalna aur mushkil ✅. (Na ke 1 electron aasani se, Mg ke 2 thoda mushkil se, Al ke 3 aur mushkil se, aur oxide ki parat bhi roke rakhti hai.)\n6. Group 13 mein B ke 2 shell, Al ke 3, Ga ke 4. Neeche utarte hue baahari electron door hota gaya aur parde ke peeche, to metallic character badha: **B < Al < Ga**. B ka electron dene ka aur lene ka vyavhaar lagbhag barabar hai, to wo seedhi par baitha **metalloid** hai.\n7. Dhatu ki reactivity group mein neeche **badhti** hai (Li < Na < K) kyunki electron dene mein aasani badhti hai. Adhaatu ki reactivity group mein neeche **ghatti** hai (F > Cl > Br > I) kyunki electron lene ki taiyari ghatti hai. Student ki baat galat: Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂ ho jaata hai par Br₂ + 2KCl → kuch nahi, to Cl₂ Br₂ se zyada reactive hai, yaani neeche Br₂ kam reactive.\n8. **LiOH < NaOH < KOH**. Group 1 mein neeche utarte hue metallic character badhta hai: dhatu electron dene mein tatpar, to hydroxide mein wo OH⁻ ko chhodne mein aasani dikhata hai, aur hydroxide zyada tez base banta hai. (Ye sab tez kshaar hain: sirf padhne ke liye.)\n9. MgO (basic), SiO₂ (kamzor acidic), P₄O₁₀ (acidic), Cl₂O₇ (bahut zyada acidic). **Increasing acidic: MgO < SiO₂ < P₄O₁₀ < Cl₂O₇**. Jaanch: Period 3 mein baayen se daayen Mg, Si, P, Cl ka order wahi hai ✅.\n10. Non-metallic: **Cl** (3 shells; Br ke 4, I ke 5). Cl mein aane wala electron nucleus ke sabse paas baithta hai, to electron lene ki kheench sabse zyada. Metallic: **Sr** (5 shells; Mg ke 3, Ca ke 4). Sr ka baahari electron sabse door aur sabse zyada shells ke parde ke peeche, to sabse aasani se nikalta hai. Jaanch: group mein neeche non-metallic character ghatta aur metallic character badhta hai ✅.\n11. (a) K ki 1 mol ke liye 419 kJ, to 5 mol ke liye 5 × 419 = **2095 kJ**. (b) Ca ke liye 5 × 590 = **2950 kJ**. (c) K ko kam energy chahiye (2095 < 2950), to **K zyada reactive**: wo electron aasani se deta hai, jo shells aur kheench ke hisaab se bhi theek hai (K ka ek hi valence electron aur kam proton). Difference 2950 − 2095 = 855 kJ. Jaanch ✅.\n12. Pehla: I₂ Br₂ se neeche hai, to uske electron lene ki taiyari kam. Doosra: I (5 shells wala) ka baahari shell Br (4 shells) se door hai, to naya electron kheenchna mushkil. Isliye **I₂ Br⁻ ko nahi nikaal sakta**; ulta Br₂ I⁻ ko nikaal sakta hai.\n13. (a) **False** ❌: Na se Cl tak metallic character **ghatta** hai. (b) **True** ✅. (c) **False** ❌: Al₂O₃ **amphoteric** hai. (d) **True** ✅. (e) **False** ❌: 2, 8, 1 wala Na hai (3 shells) aur 2, 8, 8, 1 wala K hai (4 shells); **K zyada metallic**.\n14. Configuration 2, 3: electron 5, to Z = 5, **boron (B)**. 2 shells: **Period 2**. 3 valence electrons: **Group 13**. Valency 3. **Metalloid**. Oxide B₂O₃, kamzor acidic (non-metal ki taraf). Al se **kam metallic** (group mein upar). Jaanch: B ki valency 3 aur O ki 2: B₂O₃ mein 2 × 3 = 6 = 3 × 2 ✅.\n\n---\n\nKaveri ne ghar lautkar library ke board par ek nayi line likh di: \"Dene wale = dhatu, lene wale = adhaatu, aur beech wale = metalloid.\" Mr. Yewale ne hanste hue kaha: \"Ab tum kisi bhi tatva ko dekh kar bata sakti ho ki wo library mein kis taraf baithega.\" Table mein sirf jagah dekh kar ab size, ionisation energy, dhatu-pan, reactivity aur oxide tak sab ka andaaza lagana tumhare haath mein hai.\n\n**Aage kya?** Topic 6 mein hum ye sab milkar bahut saare mixed puzzles hal karenge: ek 4-step method se \"arrange and explain\" ke sawaal, data tables, anjaan tatva ki khoj, aur ek chalk ki bani periodic table, aur poore chapter ka saar.",
            "bodyHinglish": "(Sab sawaal paper par hal karne ke liye hain; alkali metals, halogens aur tez acid ya alkali wale sawaal sirf padhne ke liye hain.)\n\n1. Arrange K, Ca and Mg in decreasing order of metallic character. Give a reason using shells and the number of electrons.\n2. Atomic number 20 is an element. Find its configuration, group, period, valency, the ion it forms, whether the ion is bigger or smaller than the atom, and the nature of its oxide.\n3. Chlorine water (Cl₂ dissolved in water) is added to separate solutions of KCl, KBr and KI. In which solutions will a reaction take place? Write the equation(s) and explain using the halogen ladder. (Fact given: Cl₂ is more reactive than Br₂ and I₂.)\n4. Name the oxide of each element with its type: Na, Al, S, P. Which one reacts with both an acid and a base?\n5. Three metals P, Q and R are Na, Mg and Al in some order. P reacts violently with cold water (teacher demo), Q reacts very slowly with cold water but faster with hot water and steam, and R does not react with cold or hot water and reacts only with steam (its oxide layer protects it). Arrange them in decreasing order of reactivity and identify each.\n6. Why does the metallic character increase from B to Al to Ga? Why is B called a metalloid?\n7. Compare the reactivity of metals and non-metals as we go down a group. A student says both increase. Show the error with examples.\n8. Arrange LiOH, NaOH and KOH in order of increasing basic strength. Give the reason in terms of metallic character.\n9. Arrange MgO, Cl₂O₇, SiO₂ and P₄O₁₀ in increasing order of acidic nature.\n10. Which is the most non-metallic element among Cl, Br and I, and which is the most metallic among Mg, Ca and Sr (strontium, just below Ca in Group 2)? Give reasons using the number of shells.\n11. The first ionisation energy of K is about 419 kJ per mol and of Ca about 590 kJ per mol. (a) How much energy is needed to remove one electron from each atom in 5 mol of K atoms? (b) The same for 5 mol of Ca atoms. (c) Which of the two metals is more reactive from this data, and why? (Gaseous atoms, first ionisation energy only.)\n12. Why is I₂ unable to take Br⁻ out of KBr, though both are halogens? Give two reasons based on the trend.\n13. State True or False and correct the false ones: (a) Metallic character increases from Na to Cl. (b) Cl₂O₇ is the most acidic oxide in Period 3. (c) Al₂O₃ is a basic oxide. (d) Reactivity of F₂ is higher than that of Cl₂. (e) An element with configuration 2, 8, 1 is more metallic than one with 2, 8, 8, 1.\n14. An element Z has configuration 2, 3. Find its group, period, valency, and whether it is metal, non-metal or metalloid. Predict whether its oxide is acidic or basic, and whether it is more or less metallic than Al.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. K: 4 shells, 1 valence electron. Ca: 4 shells, 2 valence electrons. Mg: 3 shells, 2 valence electrons. K aur Ca ke shells barabar, par Ca mein 20 protons aur K mein 19, to Ca ka kheench zyada, K sabse aasani se electron deta hai. Mg ke 3 hi shells, to electron nucleus ke paas aur kheench zyada. **K > Ca > Mg**. Jaanch: ionisation energy lagbhag 419 < 590 < 738 ✅.\n2. Z = 20: configuration **2, 8, 8, 2**. 4 shells, to **Period 4**; 2 valence electrons, **Group 2** (2 valence electron). Valency 2. Ion **Ca²⁺** (2, 8, 8, argon jaisa, 18 electron). Ion atom se **chhota** (4th shell gayi, 20 protons 18 electron ko kheench rahe hain). Oxide **CaO**, basic (Ca dhatu hai). Jaanch: CaO mein +2 aur −2 ✅. Ye element Ca hai.\n3. Cl₂ Br₂ aur I₂ dono se zyada reactive hai. **KBr aur KI** mein reaction hoga, KCl mein nahi (Cl⁻ ko Cl₂ nikaal hi nahi sakta, wo pehle se Cl hai). Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂ (K 2, Cl 2, Br 2 dono taraf ✅). Cl₂ + 2KI → 2KCl + I₂ (K 2, Cl 2, I 2 ✅). **KCl:** koi nayi cheez nahi bani.\n4. Na: **Na₂O**, basic. Al: **Al₂O₃**, amphoteric. S: **SO₃**, acidic. P: **P₄O₁₀**, acidic. **Al₂O₃** acid aur base dono se reaction karta hai (Al₂O₃ + 6HCl → 2AlCl₃ + 3H₂O aur Al₂O₃ + 2NaOH → 2NaAlO₂ + H₂O). Jaanch: Al 2, O 3, H 6, Cl 6 dono taraf ✅.\n5. Reactivity: P > Q > R. Period 3 mein baayen se daayen reactivity ghatti hai, to **P = Na, Q = Mg, R = Al**. Jaanch: ionisation energy lagbhag Na 496 < Mg 738, aur Al ke 3 electron ko nikalna aur mushkil ✅. (Na ke 1 electron aasani se, Mg ke 2 thoda mushkil se, Al ke 3 aur mushkil se, aur oxide ki parat bhi roke rakhti hai.)\n6. Group 13 mein B ke 2 shell, Al ke 3, Ga ke 4. Neeche utarte hue baahari electron door hota gaya aur parde ke peeche, to metallic character badha: **B < Al < Ga**. B ka electron dene ka aur lene ka vyavhaar lagbhag barabar hai, to wo seedhi par baitha **metalloid** hai.\n7. Dhatu ki reactivity group mein neeche **badhti** hai (Li < Na < K) kyunki electron dene mein aasani badhti hai. Adhaatu ki reactivity group mein neeche **ghatti** hai (F > Cl > Br > I) kyunki electron lene ki taiyari ghatti hai. Student ki baat galat: Cl₂ + 2KBr → 2KCl + Br₂ ho jaata hai par Br₂ + 2KCl → kuch nahi, to Cl₂ Br₂ se zyada reactive hai, yaani neeche Br₂ kam reactive.\n8. **LiOH < NaOH < KOH**. Group 1 mein neeche utarte hue metallic character badhta hai: dhatu electron dene mein tatpar, to hydroxide mein wo OH⁻ ko chhodne mein aasani dikhata hai, aur hydroxide zyada tez base banta hai. (Ye sab tez kshaar hain: sirf padhne ke liye.)\n9. MgO (basic), SiO₂ (kamzor acidic), P₄O₁₀ (acidic), Cl₂O₇ (bahut zyada acidic). **Increasing acidic: MgO < SiO₂ < P₄O₁₀ < Cl₂O₇**. Jaanch: Period 3 mein baayen se daayen Mg, Si, P, Cl ka order wahi hai ✅.\n10. Non-metallic: **Cl** (3 shells; Br ke 4, I ke 5). Cl mein aane wala electron nucleus ke sabse paas baithta hai, to electron lene ki kheench sabse zyada. Metallic: **Sr** (5 shells; Mg ke 3, Ca ke 4). Sr ka baahari electron sabse door aur sabse zyada shells ke parde ke peeche, to sabse aasani se nikalta hai. Jaanch: group mein neeche non-metallic character ghatta aur metallic character badhta hai ✅.\n11. (a) K ki 1 mol ke liye 419 kJ, to 5 mol ke liye 5 × 419 = **2095 kJ**. (b) Ca ke liye 5 × 590 = **2950 kJ**. (c) K ko kam energy chahiye (2095 < 2950), to **K zyada reactive**: wo electron aasani se deta hai, jo shells aur kheench ke hisaab se bhi theek hai (K ka ek hi valence electron aur kam proton). Difference 2950 − 2095 = 855 kJ. Jaanch ✅.\n12. Pehla: I₂ Br₂ se neeche hai, to uske electron lene ki taiyari kam. Doosra: I (5 shells wala) ka baahari shell Br (4 shells) se door hai, to naya electron kheenchna mushkil. Isliye **I₂ Br⁻ ko nahi nikaal sakta**; ulta Br₂ I⁻ ko nikaal sakta hai.\n13. (a) **False** ❌: Na se Cl tak metallic character **ghatta** hai. (b) **True** ✅. (c) **False** ❌: Al₂O₃ **amphoteric** hai. (d) **True** ✅. (e) **False** ❌: 2, 8, 1 wala Na hai (3 shells) aur 2, 8, 8, 1 wala K hai (4 shells); **K zyada metallic**.\n14. Configuration 2, 3: electron 5, to Z = 5, **boron (B)**. 2 shells: **Period 2**. 3 valence electrons: **Group 13**. Valency 3. **Metalloid**. Oxide B₂O₃, kamzor acidic (non-metal ki taraf). Al se **kam metallic** (group mein upar). Jaanch: B ki valency 3 aur O ki 2: B₂O₃ mein 2 × 3 = 6 = 3 × 2 ✅.\n\n---\n\nKaveri ne ghar lautkar library ke board par ek nayi line likh di: \"Dene wale = dhatu, lene wale = adhaatu, aur beech wale = metalloid.\" Mr. Yewale ne hanste hue kaha: \"Ab tum kisi bhi tatva ko dekh kar bata sakti ho ki wo library mein kis taraf baithega.\" Table mein sirf jagah dekh kar ab size, ionisation energy, dhatu-pan, reactivity aur oxide tak sab ka andaaza lagana tumhare haath mein hai.\n\n**Aage kya?** Topic 6 mein hum ye sab milkar bahut saare mixed puzzles hal karenge: ek 4-step method se \"arrange and explain\" ke sawaal, data tables, anjaan tatva ki khoj, aur ek chalk ki bani periodic table, aur poore chapter ka saar."
          }
