            "body": "Itwaar ki subah thi. School ke Science Club ne maidan par ek khaas kaam rakha tha: zameen par chalk se ek bada periodic table banana, aur bacchon ko khud \"tatva\" banakar uske andar khade hona. Club ke in-charge Mr. Lokhande ne apni bhatiji Tanuja ko bhi saath bula liya tha. Tanuja Class 10 mein padhti thi aur ghar mein unhein \"Chacha\" kehti thi; maidan mein bhi wahi naam chal gaya, jise sunkar baaki bacche muskura diye.\n\nChacha ne kehte hue ek lambi rassi se pehli row naapi. \"Aaj humein sirf pehle 18 tatva banane hain: teen rows. Har dabba 1 metre ka.\" Bacche chalk lekar dabbe kheenchne lage, aur Tanuja ne har dabbe mein symbol likha. Jab table taiyaar hua to Chacha ne ek ajeeb sawaal poocha: \"Agar main Na ke dabbe se Cl ke dabbe tak chalu, to mere saath kaun-kaun si cheezein badlengi? Aur agar main Li ke dabbe se seedha neeche K ki taraf utru?\"\n\nTanuja ne turant jawab dena chaha, par phir ruk gayi. Chapter ke paanchon topic ek-ek karke uske dimaag mein ghoom gaye, par jawab ek line mein nahi aa raha tha. Chacha ne hanste hue kaha: \"Yahi to dikkat hai. Jaankari hai, par use **kramwar** lagana nahi aata. Chalo, ek tareeka banate hain: kisi bhi sawaal ke liye, chaar kadam.\"\n\n```\n   Group:  1    2   13   14   15   16   17   18\n\n   P1      H                                  He\n   P2      Li   Be   B    C    N    O    F    Ne\n   P3      Na   Mg   Al   Si   P    S    Cl   Ar\n```\n\n> **Figure 6.1** – Maidan ke chalk-table ka naksha: pehle 18 tatva, 3 periods (rows) aur 8 columns (Group 1, 2 aur 13 se 18). Beech ke Group 3 se 12 (transition metals) is chhote naksha mein chhod diye gaye hain. Period 1 mein sirf H aur He hain, isliye beech ke dabbe khaali hain.",
