            "correctIndex": 3,
            "explanation": "Pitfall to avoid (\"Do alag atom ke beech ka bond hamesha polar hota hai.\"): Sach: bond ka swabhav farq par depend karta hai, \"alag atom\" hone par nahi. Demo: P (2.1) aur H (2.1) alag tatva hain, par farq 0.0 hai: PH₃ (phosphine, ek zehreeli gas: sirf padhne ke liye) ke P–H bond bilkul non-polar jaise hain. C (2.5) aur H (2.1) ka farq sirf 0.4 hai: lagbhag non-polar. S (2.5) aur H (2.1) ka farq bhi 0.4 hai. Ab sirf farq badhao: H–Cl (0.9) aur H–F (1.9): ye saaf polar hain. Matlab \"alag atom\" se bond polar nahi banta; kheench ka farq polar banata hai.",
