            "heading": "Part C: Pb²⁺ aur Al³⁺: NH₄OH ke saath twins",
            "headingHinglish": "Part C: Pb²⁺ aur Al³⁺: NH₄OH ke saath twins",
            "body": "Topic 2 mein dekha tha ki Pb²⁺ aur Al³⁺ dono NaOH ke saath safed precipitate dete hain jo excess NaOH mein ghul jaata hai. NH₄OH ke saath bhi dono **safed precipitate** dete hain, aur dono **excess NH₄OH mein nahi ghulte**. Yaani NH₄OH inhe bhi **alag nahi kar pata**. Twin jaisi pehchaan!\n\n**Lead acetate: zehreela (sirf dekhne ke liye).** Is topic mein lead ka ghulansheel namak **lead acetate, (CH₃COO)₂Pb** liya hai. Lead ke saare namak **zehreele** hain: koi student unhe haath nahi lagata, chakhta nahi, aur kachra teacher sambhalta hai. Aluminium ke liye **AlCl₃** lete hain.\n\n(CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2NH₄OH → Pb(OH)₂↓ + 2CH₃COONH₄\nAlCl₃ + 3NH₄OH → Al(OH)₃↓ + 3NH₄Cl\n\n**Jaanch:** Pb: Pb 1 = 1, C 4 = 4, H 6 + 10 = 16 = 2 + 14 = 16, O 4 + 2 = 6 = 2 + 4 = 6, N 2 = 2 ✅. Al: Al 1 = 1, Cl 3 = 3, N 3 = 3, H 15 = 3 + 12 = 15, O 3 = 3 ✅.\n\n```\n   Tube 1              Tube 2              Tube 3\n   :              :    :              :    :              :\n   :   Pb ghol    :    :   Al ghol    :    :   Zn ghol    :\n   :   + NH₄OH    :    :   + NH₄OH    :    :   + NH₄OH    :\n   :    zyada     :    :    zyada     :    :    zyada     :\n   :              :    :              :    :              :\n   :  ##########  :    :  ##########  :    :  (ppt nahi)  :\n   '--------------'    '--------------'    '--------------'\n```\n\n> **Figure 3.4** – Excess NH₄OH ke baad: Pb²⁺ (Tube 1) aur Al³⁺ (Tube 2) dono mein safed precipitate neeche (# nishan) bacha hai, jabki Zn²⁺ (Tube 3) mein precipitate ghul gaya. Pb aur Al ko NH₄OH se alag nahi kiya ja sakta, Zn ko kiya ja sakta hai.\n\n### Example 6. Pb²⁺ aur Al³⁺ ko alag kaise karein?\n\nDono ke tube mein ek jaisa safed precipitate hai, to ek **alag test** chahiye. Lead ke ghol ki ek aur pehchaan hai (sirf padhne ke liye, teacher demo):\n\n- Lead acetate ke ghol mein **dilute HCl** ki kuch boond: **safed precipitate PbCl₂**. (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2HCl → PbCl₂↓ + 2CH₃COOH. AlCl₃ ke ghol mein koi precipitate nahi banta (Al ka chloride ghulansheel hai).\n- Lead acetate mein **potassium iodide (KI)** ki boond: **chamkeela peela precipitate PbI₂** (Class 9 ka \"golden rain\" wala teacher demo yaad hai? Wahi PbI₂). (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2KI → PbI₂↓ + 2CH₃COOK. Al ke ghol mein peela precipitate nahi aata.\n\nLead ke ye saare precipitate bhi zehreele hain, to sirf teacher ke haath se hote hain.\n**Jaanch:** (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2HCl: Pb 1 = 1, C 4 = 4, H 6 + 2 = 8 = 8, O 4 = 4, Cl 2 = 2 ✅. (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2KI: Pb 1 = 1, K 2 = 2, I 2 = 2, C 4 = 4, H 6 = 6, O 4 = 4 ✅.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Topic 2 mein dekha tha ki Pb²⁺ aur Al³⁺ dono NaOH ke saath safed precipitate dete hain jo excess NaOH mein ghul jaata hai. NH₄OH ke saath bhi dono **safed precipitate** dete hain, aur dono **excess NH₄OH mein nahi ghulte**. Yaani NH₄OH inhe bhi **alag nahi kar pata**. Twin jaisi pehchaan!\n\n**Lead acetate: zehreela (sirf dekhne ke liye).** Is topic mein lead ka ghulansheel namak **lead acetate, (CH₃COO)₂Pb** liya hai. Lead ke saare namak **zehreele** hain: koi student unhe haath nahi lagata, chakhta nahi, aur kachra teacher sambhalta hai. Aluminium ke liye **AlCl₃** lete hain.\n\n(CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2NH₄OH → Pb(OH)₂↓ + 2CH₃COONH₄\nAlCl₃ + 3NH₄OH → Al(OH)₃↓ + 3NH₄Cl\n\n**Jaanch:** Pb: Pb 1 = 1, C 4 = 4, H 6 + 10 = 16 = 2 + 14 = 16, O 4 + 2 = 6 = 2 + 4 = 6, N 2 = 2 ✅. Al: Al 1 = 1, Cl 3 = 3, N 3 = 3, H 15 = 3 + 12 = 15, O 3 = 3 ✅.\n\n```\n   Tube 1              Tube 2              Tube 3\n   :              :    :              :    :              :\n   :   Pb ghol    :    :   Al ghol    :    :   Zn ghol    :\n   :   + NH₄OH    :    :   + NH₄OH    :    :   + NH₄OH    :\n   :    zyada     :    :    zyada     :    :    zyada     :\n   :              :    :              :    :              :\n   :  ##########  :    :  ##########  :    :  (ppt nahi)  :\n   '--------------'    '--------------'    '--------------'\n```\n\n> **Figure 3.4** – Excess NH₄OH ke baad: Pb²⁺ (Tube 1) aur Al³⁺ (Tube 2) dono mein safed precipitate neeche (# nishan) bacha hai, jabki Zn²⁺ (Tube 3) mein precipitate ghul gaya. Pb aur Al ko NH₄OH se alag nahi kiya ja sakta, Zn ko kiya ja sakta hai.\n\n### Example 6. Pb²⁺ aur Al³⁺ ko alag kaise karein?\n\nDono ke tube mein ek jaisa safed precipitate hai, to ek **alag test** chahiye. Lead ke ghol ki ek aur pehchaan hai (sirf padhne ke liye, teacher demo):\n\n- Lead acetate ke ghol mein **dilute HCl** ki kuch boond: **safed precipitate PbCl₂**. (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2HCl → PbCl₂↓ + 2CH₃COOH. AlCl₃ ke ghol mein koi precipitate nahi banta (Al ka chloride ghulansheel hai).\n- Lead acetate mein **potassium iodide (KI)** ki boond: **chamkeela peela precipitate PbI₂** (Class 9 ka \"golden rain\" wala teacher demo yaad hai? Wahi PbI₂). (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2KI → PbI₂↓ + 2CH₃COOK. Al ke ghol mein peela precipitate nahi aata.\n\nLead ke ye saare precipitate bhi zehreele hain, to sirf teacher ke haath se hote hain.\n**Jaanch:** (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2HCl: Pb 1 = 1, C 4 = 4, H 6 + 2 = 8 = 8, O 4 = 4, Cl 2 = 2 ✅. (CH₃COO)₂Pb + 2KI: Pb 1 = 1, K 2 = 2, I 2 = 2, C 4 = 4, H 6 = 6, O 4 = 4 ✅."
