            "body": "Ek baarish ke baad Mr. Vaze apni bhanji Sukanya ko school ki chemistry lab ke store room mein le gaye. Chhutti ka din tha, aur wo lab-in-charge teacher the. Khidki ki daraar se paani andar aaya tha, aur almirah ki neeche wali shelf par rakhi botalon ke label geele hokar gal gaye the. Chaar botalon par kuchh bhi padha nahi ja raha tha.\n\nSukanya ne goggles pehne aur tape se bani line ke peeche khadi ho gayi (student lab mein sirf teacher ke saath, aur teacher ke dene par hi kuch chhoote). \"Mama, ab kya karenge? Chakh kar dekh lein?\" Mr. Vaze hans pade. \"Kabhi nahi. Chemistry mein kisi cheez ko chakhna, soongna ya haath lagana jasoosi nahi, bewakoofi hai. Hum **tests** se pata lagayenge. Pehle dekhenge, phir ghulenge, phir cation, phir anion.\"\n\n\"Par Mama, kitne tests karne padenge?\" \"Utne hi, jitne sawaal hain. Har test ek sawaal ka jawab deta hai: ye kaun sa ion hai? Aur ek bottle ki saari jaankari ek hi test se nahi milti.\"\n\n```\n   Shelf par chaar botal (label gal gaye):\n\n    [ ? ]      [ ? ]      [ ? ]      [ ? ]\n    botal 1    botal 2    botal 3    botal 4\n    peela-     halka      neela      rangheen\n    bhura      hara       ghol       ghol\n    ghol       ghol                  (paani jaisa)\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.1** – Store room ki shelf: chaar botal, label nahi. Pehla kadam bina chhue sirf **dekhna** hai: ghol ka rang. Is ghol ke rang se aage ke tests ki disha milti hai, par poora jawab nahi.\n\nChaaron botalon ka sahi jawab aaj ke topic mein ek-ek karke nikalenge.",
