            "body": "Kuchh ions ke tests lagbhag ek jaise lagte hain. Unhe alag karne ka sabse chhota tareeka ek jodi ke liye ek hi test hota hai.\n\n| Jodi | Alag karne wala test | Kya dikhega |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fe²⁺ aur Fe³⁺ | Ghol ka rang ya NaOH ka precipitate | Gande hare ya laal-bhura |\n| Zn²⁺ aur Al³⁺ | Excess NH₄OH | Zn²⁺ ghulta hai, Al³⁺ nahi |\n| Pb²⁺ aur Al³⁺ | KI ki boondein (padhne ke liye) | Pb²⁺ se peela precipitate, Al³⁺ se nahi |\n| Ca²⁺ aur Zn²⁺ | Excess NaOH | Zn²⁺ ghulta hai, Ca²⁺ nahi |\n\n```\n   Ghol rangheen: NaOH ki boondein, phir excess\n                     :\n         +-----------+------------+\n         :                        :\n     precipitate ghula         nahi ghula\n         :                        :\n   Zn, Pb ya Al                  Ca²⁺\n         :\n   NH₄OH excess\n         :\n   +-----+------+\n   :            :\n ghula       nahi ghula\n   :            :\n  Zn²⁺      Pb ya Al\n                :\n              KI test\n```\n\n> **Figure 5.4** – Rangheen ghol ke liye cation ka flowchart: pehle NaOH ki boondein aur excess, phir NH₄OH excess, aakhir mein KI. Har mod par ek hi sawaal.",
