            "heading": "Part D: Kitna dhodha banega? (Chapter 5 ka mole method)",
            "headingHinglish": "Part D: Kitna dhodha banega? (Chapter 5 ka mole method)",
            "body": "### Example 1. Cu(NO₃)₂ aur NaOH se dhodhe ka mass\n\n**Sawaal:** **18.75 g** Cu(NO₃)₂ ke ghol mein NaOH ki bilkul zaroori matra daali gayi. Kitna Cu(OH)₂ ka dhodha banega, aur ghol mein kitna NaNO₃ rahega? (Cu = 63.5, N = 14, O = 16, H = 1, Na = 23.)\n\n**Equation:** Cu(NO₃)₂ + 2NaOH → Cu(OH)₂↓ + 2NaNO₃\n\n**Kadam 1 (molar mass):** Cu(NO₃)₂ = 63.5 + 2 × (14 + 3 × 16) = 63.5 + 2 × 62 = **187.5 g/mol**. Cu(OH)₂ = 63.5 + 2 × 17 = **97.5 g/mol**. NaNO₃ = 23 + 14 + 48 = **85 g/mol**.\n**Kadam 2 (mole):** 18.75 ÷ 187.5 = **0.1 mol**.\n**Kadam 3 (ratio):** 1 mol Cu(NO₃)₂ se 1 mol Cu(OH)₂ aur 2 mol NaNO₃. To 0.1 mol se 0.1 mol Cu(OH)₂ aur 0.2 mol NaNO₃.\n**Kadam 4 (mass):** Cu(OH)₂ = 0.1 × 97.5 = **9.75 g**. NaNO₃ = 0.2 × 85 = **17 g**.\n\n```\n       :  saaf ghol (NaNO₃ ghula)  :\n       :                           :\n       :   Cu(OH)₂ dhodha : 9.75 g :\n       :___________________________:\n```\n\n> **Figure 6.6** – Test tube: Cu(OH)₂ ka halka neela dhodha neeche baitha hai, upar saaf ghol mein NaNO₃ ghula hai.\n\n**Jaanch:** NaOH ka mass = 0.2 mol × 40 = 8 g. Left: 18.75 + 8 = 26.75 g. Right: 9.75 + 17 = 26.75 g ✅ (mass conservation).\n\n(Ye numerical sirf \"kitna dhodha\" jaanne ke liye hai; asli lab mein aisa tola-bhar kaam teacher hi karta hai.)",
            "bodyHinglish": "### Example 1. Cu(NO₃)₂ aur NaOH se dhodhe ka mass\n\n**Sawaal:** **18.75 g** Cu(NO₃)₂ ke ghol mein NaOH ki bilkul zaroori matra daali gayi. Kitna Cu(OH)₂ ka dhodha banega, aur ghol mein kitna NaNO₃ rahega? (Cu = 63.5, N = 14, O = 16, H = 1, Na = 23.)\n\n**Equation:** Cu(NO₃)₂ + 2NaOH → Cu(OH)₂↓ + 2NaNO₃\n\n**Kadam 1 (molar mass):** Cu(NO₃)₂ = 63.5 + 2 × (14 + 3 × 16) = 63.5 + 2 × 62 = **187.5 g/mol**. Cu(OH)₂ = 63.5 + 2 × 17 = **97.5 g/mol**. NaNO₃ = 23 + 14 + 48 = **85 g/mol**.\n**Kadam 2 (mole):** 18.75 ÷ 187.5 = **0.1 mol**.\n**Kadam 3 (ratio):** 1 mol Cu(NO₃)₂ se 1 mol Cu(OH)₂ aur 2 mol NaNO₃. To 0.1 mol se 0.1 mol Cu(OH)₂ aur 0.2 mol NaNO₃.\n**Kadam 4 (mass):** Cu(OH)₂ = 0.1 × 97.5 = **9.75 g**. NaNO₃ = 0.2 × 85 = **17 g**.\n\n```\n       :  saaf ghol (NaNO₃ ghula)  :\n       :                           :\n       :   Cu(OH)₂ dhodha : 9.75 g :\n       :___________________________:\n```\n\n> **Figure 6.6** – Test tube: Cu(OH)₂ ka halka neela dhodha neeche baitha hai, upar saaf ghol mein NaNO₃ ghula hai.\n\n**Jaanch:** NaOH ka mass = 0.2 mol × 40 = 8 g. Left: 18.75 + 8 = 26.75 g. Right: 9.75 + 17 = 26.75 g ✅ (mass conservation).\n\n(Ye numerical sirf \"kitna dhodha\" jaanne ke liye hai; asli lab mein aisa tola-bhar kaam teacher hi karta hai.)"
