          {
            "heading": "Part E: Ammonia khet tak: khaad",
            "headingHinglish": "Part E: Ammonia khet tak: khaad",
            "body": "Ammonia gas ko seedha zameen mein daalna mushkil hai, isliye use acid se milakar **ammonium namak** banate hain, jo ghulkar paudhon ko NH₄⁺ ya nitrate dete hain:\n\n2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄ (ammonium sulphate)\nNH₃ + HNO₃ → NH₄NO₃ (ammonium nitrate: HNO₃ ki kahani Topic 3 mein)\n\nTeesri khaad **urea** CO(NH₂)₂ bhi ammonia se banti hai (formula yaad rakho, uska banne ka tareeka aage ki class mein). Class 9 mein humne in teeno mein nitrogen ka percent nikala tha; ab hum inse ammonia ka hisaab nikalenge.\n\n```\n   N₂ (hawa) + H₂\n        :\n        v\n   NH₃ --+--> + H₂SO₄ --> (NH₄)₂SO₄\n         :\n         +--> + HNO₃  --> NH₄NO₃\n         :\n         +--> urea CO(NH₂)₂\n         :\n         +--> HNO₃ banane ke liye (Topic 3)\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.6** – Ammonia kaise-kaise khaad mein badalti hai. Neeche wali shaakha Topic 3 ki taraf jaati hai.\n\n### Example 5. Khaad ke liye ammonia\n\n**Sawaal:** 264 kg (NH₄)₂SO₄ banane ke liye kitni NH₃ lagegi? (NH₄)₂SO₄ ka M = 2 × 18 + 96 = 132.\n\n**Kadam 1:** 264 ÷ 132 = **2 kmol**. **Kadam 2 (ratio 2NH₃ : 1):** NH₃ = 4 kmol = 4 × 17 = **68 kg**.\n\n**Jaanch:** acid H₂SO₄ = 2 kmol × 98 = 196 kg; 68 + 196 = 264 ✅.\n\n### Example 6. NH₄NO₃ ke liye ammonia\n\n**Sawaal:** 400 kg NH₄NO₃ ke liye kitni NH₃? NH₄NO₃ ka M = 14 + 4 + 14 + 48 = 80.\n\n400 ÷ 80 = **5 kmol**, ratio 1 : 1, NH₃ = 5 × 17 = **85 kg**.\n\n**Jaanch:** 85 kg + HNO₃ (5 × 63 = 315 kg) = 400 kg ✅.\n\n**Aur upyog:** nitric acid banana (Topic 3), thande bhandar ka refrigeration (liquid ammonia ke bhaap banne par thandak), aur ghar ke safai wale ghol (dilute NH₄OH: **bachche kabhi na chhuen**, bleach ya toilet cleaner ke saath kabhi nahi milana).",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ammonia gas ko seedha zameen mein daalna mushkil hai, isliye use acid se milakar **ammonium namak** banate hain, jo ghulkar paudhon ko NH₄⁺ ya nitrate dete hain:\n\n2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄ (ammonium sulphate)\nNH₃ + HNO₃ → NH₄NO₃ (ammonium nitrate: HNO₃ ki kahani Topic 3 mein)\n\nTeesri khaad **urea** CO(NH₂)₂ bhi ammonia se banti hai (formula yaad rakho, uska banne ka tareeka aage ki class mein). Class 9 mein humne in teeno mein nitrogen ka percent nikala tha; ab hum inse ammonia ka hisaab nikalenge.\n\n```\n   N₂ (hawa) + H₂\n        :\n        v\n   NH₃ --+--> + H₂SO₄ --> (NH₄)₂SO₄\n         :\n         +--> + HNO₃  --> NH₄NO₃\n         :\n         +--> urea CO(NH₂)₂\n         :\n         +--> HNO₃ banane ke liye (Topic 3)\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.6** – Ammonia kaise-kaise khaad mein badalti hai. Neeche wali shaakha Topic 3 ki taraf jaati hai.\n\n### Example 5. Khaad ke liye ammonia\n\n**Sawaal:** 264 kg (NH₄)₂SO₄ banane ke liye kitni NH₃ lagegi? (NH₄)₂SO₄ ka M = 2 × 18 + 96 = 132.\n\n**Kadam 1:** 264 ÷ 132 = **2 kmol**. **Kadam 2 (ratio 2NH₃ : 1):** NH₃ = 4 kmol = 4 × 17 = **68 kg**.\n\n**Jaanch:** acid H₂SO₄ = 2 kmol × 98 = 196 kg; 68 + 196 = 264 ✅.\n\n### Example 6. NH₄NO₃ ke liye ammonia\n\n**Sawaal:** 400 kg NH₄NO₃ ke liye kitni NH₃? NH₄NO₃ ka M = 14 + 4 + 14 + 48 = 80.\n\n400 ÷ 80 = **5 kmol**, ratio 1 : 1, NH₃ = 5 × 17 = **85 kg**.\n\n**Jaanch:** 85 kg + HNO₃ (5 × 63 = 315 kg) = 400 kg ✅.\n\n**Aur upyog:** nitric acid banana (Topic 3), thande bhandar ka refrigeration (liquid ammonia ke bhaap banne par thandak), aur ghar ke safai wale ghol (dilute NH₄OH: **bachche kabhi na chhuen**, bleach ya toilet cleaner ke saath kabhi nahi milana)."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti: \"Ammonia ko conc. H₂SO₄ se dry kar sakte hain, aur paani ke upar jama kar sakte hain.\"**\nHCl ke liye ye dono sahi lagte hain, isliye ammonia ke liye bhi laga dena aasaan hai. Par dono galat hain. Do chhote demo (sirf padhne ke liye):\n\n**Demo 1: conc. H₂SO₄ mein se gas guzaarna.**\n\n```\n   Ammonia aayi --> .-------------.   --> gas jar mein kuch nahi aata\n                    : conc. H₂SO₄ :\n                    :  (wash bottle)\n                    :_____________:\n     bottle mein ab (NH₄)₂SO₄ ban gaya, gas khatam\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.7** – Galat tareeka: ammonia wash bottle ki conc. H₂SO₄ se reaction karke namak ban gayi, isliye bottle ke doosre taraf kuch gas nahi nikli.\n\nEquation: 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄. Gas **sookhi** nahi hui, **gayab** ho gayi. Anhydrous CaCl₂ ke saath bhi yahi dikkat hai (ye ammonia ko jakad leta hai).\n\n**Demo 2: paani ke upar jama karna.** Maan lo ek 1 L ki jar paani ke upar ulti rakhi hai aur usme ammonia bhari ja rahi hai. 1 volume paani mein lagbhag 700 volume NH₃ ghul sakti hai, to trough ka thoda sa paani bhi jar mein aane wali saari gas ko turant kha jaata hai. Jar ke andar dabaav gir jaata hai aur **paani jar mein chadh jaata hai** (fountain jaisa). Gas jama hi nahi hoti.\n\n| Gas | Sookhane ke liye | Bharne ke liye |\n|---|---|---|\n| HCl (Topic 1) | conc. H₂SO₄ | upward displacement of air |\n| NH₃ (aaj) | quicklime CaO | downward displacement of air |\n\n**Niyam:** gas ki **prakriti** (acidic ya basic) dekho aur uske hisaab se drier chuno. Aur gas ki **ghulansheelta** dekho: bahut ghulansheel gas paani ke upar jama nahi hoti.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti: \"Ammonia ko conc. H₂SO₄ se dry kar sakte hain, aur paani ke upar jama kar sakte hain.\"**\nHCl ke liye ye dono sahi lagte hain, isliye ammonia ke liye bhi laga dena aasaan hai. Par dono galat hain. Do chhote demo (sirf padhne ke liye):\n\n**Demo 1: conc. H₂SO₄ mein se gas guzaarna.**\n\n```\n   Ammonia aayi --> .-------------.   --> gas jar mein kuch nahi aata\n                    : conc. H₂SO₄ :\n                    :  (wash bottle)\n                    :_____________:\n     bottle mein ab (NH₄)₂SO₄ ban gaya, gas khatam\n```\n\n> **Figure 2.7** – Galat tareeka: ammonia wash bottle ki conc. H₂SO₄ se reaction karke namak ban gayi, isliye bottle ke doosre taraf kuch gas nahi nikli.\n\nEquation: 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄. Gas **sookhi** nahi hui, **gayab** ho gayi. Anhydrous CaCl₂ ke saath bhi yahi dikkat hai (ye ammonia ko jakad leta hai).\n\n**Demo 2: paani ke upar jama karna.** Maan lo ek 1 L ki jar paani ke upar ulti rakhi hai aur usme ammonia bhari ja rahi hai. 1 volume paani mein lagbhag 700 volume NH₃ ghul sakti hai, to trough ka thoda sa paani bhi jar mein aane wali saari gas ko turant kha jaata hai. Jar ke andar dabaav gir jaata hai aur **paani jar mein chadh jaata hai** (fountain jaisa). Gas jama hi nahi hoti.\n\n| Gas | Sookhane ke liye | Bharne ke liye |\n|---|---|---|\n| HCl (Topic 1) | conc. H₂SO₄ | upward displacement of air |\n| NH₃ (aaj) | quicklime CaO | downward displacement of air |\n\n**Niyam:** gas ki **prakriti** (acidic ya basic) dekho aur uske hisaab se drier chuno. Aur gas ki **ghulansheelta** dekho: bahut ghulansheel gas paani ke upar jama nahi hoti."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- Lab preparation: 2NH₄Cl + Ca(OH)₂ → CaCl₂ + 2H₂O + 2NH₃, sookha mishran, tube ka mooh halka neeche.\n- Sookhane ke liye **CaO**, conc. H₂SO₄ ya CaCl₂ nahi: ye ammonia ko kha jaate hain.\n- Ammonia hawa se halki (V.D. 8.5 vs lagbhag 14.5): **downward displacement of air**, ulta jar, tube upar tak. Paani ke upar nahi, kyunki bahut ghulansheel.\n- NH₃ + H₂O ⇌ NH₄OH, kamzor base: moist red litmus neela.\n- Fountain experiment dikhata hai ki NH₃ bahut ghulansheel aur ghol alkaline hai.\n- Reactions: HCl se safed dhuan, oxygen mein jalna, Pt par 4NH₃ + 5O₂ → 4NO + 6H₂O, chlorine se NH₄Cl aur N₂.\n- Haber: N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃, iron catalyst, lagbhag 200 atm, lagbhag 450 °C, shartein samjhauta hain, bina badli gas recycle hoti hai.\n- Upyog: khaad (ammonium sulphate, ammonium nitrate, urea), nitric acid, refrigeration, safai ke ghol.\n- Ammonia zehreeli hai: sab kuch sirf padhne ke liye ya teacher demo.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- Lab preparation: 2NH₄Cl + Ca(OH)₂ → CaCl₂ + 2H₂O + 2NH₃, sookha mishran, tube ka mooh halka neeche.\n- Sookhane ke liye **CaO**, conc. H₂SO₄ ya CaCl₂ nahi: ye ammonia ko kha jaate hain.\n- Ammonia hawa se halki (V.D. 8.5 vs lagbhag 14.5): **downward displacement of air**, ulta jar, tube upar tak. Paani ke upar nahi, kyunki bahut ghulansheel.\n- NH₃ + H₂O ⇌ NH₄OH, kamzor base: moist red litmus neela.\n- Fountain experiment dikhata hai ki NH₃ bahut ghulansheel aur ghol alkaline hai.\n- Reactions: HCl se safed dhuan, oxygen mein jalna, Pt par 4NH₃ + 5O₂ → 4NO + 6H₂O, chlorine se NH₄Cl aur N₂.\n- Haber: N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃, iron catalyst, lagbhag 200 atm, lagbhag 450 °C, shartein samjhauta hain, bina badli gas recycle hoti hai.\n- Upyog: khaad (ammonium sulphate, ammonium nitrate, urea), nitric acid, refrigeration, safai ke ghol.\n- Ammonia zehreeli hai: sab kuch sirf padhne ke liye ya teacher demo."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "(Mass: H 1, C 12, N 14, O 16, S 32, Cl 35.5, Ca 40. Molar volume 22.4 L at STP.)\n\n1. A teacher heats 42.8 g of NH₄Cl with enough Ca(OH)₂. Find the mass of Ca(OH)₂ used, the mass of CaCl₂ formed, and the volume of NH₃ at STP.\n2. What mass of NH₄Cl must be heated with excess Ca(OH)₂ to obtain 6.72 L of ammonia at STP?\n3. Explain why the test tube used to prepare ammonia from NH₄Cl and Ca(OH)₂ is tilted with its mouth slightly downward.\n4. Ammonia is passed through each of (a) conc. H₂SO₄, (b) quicklime. For each, say whether ammonia is dried and write any equation.\n5. How many kg of urea contain 70 kg of nitrogen? (Use the formula CO(NH₂)₂.)\n6. A farmer needs the same amount of nitrogen as is present in 120 kg of urea, but wants to use NH₄NO₃ instead. How many kg of NH₄NO₃ is needed?\n7. How many kg of NH₃ and of H₂SO₄ are needed to make 33 kg of (NH₄)₂SO₄ by 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄?\n8. A bag of fertiliser is labelled \"N 46 percent\". A field needs 23 kg of nitrogen. How many kg of that fertiliser is needed?\n9. 3.4 g of NH₃ reacts completely with HCl gas to form white fumes. Find the mass of HCl used and the mass of NH₄Cl formed.\n10. 20.4 g of NH₃ burns completely in oxygen as 4NH₃ + 3O₂ → 2N₂ + 6H₂O. Find the volume of oxygen used at STP.\n11. In a Haber plant, 51 kg of NH₃ is made by N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃ (ideal case). Find the masses of N₂ and H₂ used. Then explain why plants run at about 450 °C and not at 100 °C, given that \"a lower temperature gives a larger share of ammonia in the mixture but the reaction becomes very slow\".\n12. Choose and justify: which gas jar position (upright or inverted) and which method collects ammonia, and why can it not be collected over water? What would be seen if a student tried?\n13. State True or False and correct the false ones: (a) Ammonia is dried with conc. H₂SO₄. (b) NH₃ is lighter than air. (c) A catalyst increases the amount of ammonia in the Haber mixture. (d) Dry NH₃ turns dry red litmus blue. (e) NH₄Cl, (NH₄)₂SO₄ and NH₄NO₃ are all made from ammonia.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. NH₄Cl = 53.5 g/mol, 42.8 ÷ 53.5 = **0.8 mol**. Ratio 2 : 1 : 1 : 2: Ca(OH)₂ = 0.4 mol × 74 = **29.6 g**; CaCl₂ = 0.4 × 111 = **44.4 g**; NH₃ = 0.8 mol, 0.8 × 22.4 = **17.92 L**. Jaanch: H₂O = 0.8 mol = 14.4 g, NH₃ = 0.8 × 17 = 13.6 g; reactants 42.8 + 29.6 = 72.4; products 44.4 + 14.4 + 13.6 = 72.4 ✅.\n2. 6.72 ÷ 22.4 = **0.3 mol** NH₃. Ratio 1 : 1 to NH₄Cl, to 0.3 mol = 0.3 × 53.5 = **16.05 g**. Jaanch: 16.05 ÷ 53.5 = 0.3 ✅.\n3. Reaction mein paani banta hai jo test tube ke thande mooh par boond bankar wapas garam tale ki taraf behne ki koshish karta hai. Mooh neeche hone se wo bahar nikal jaata hai aur garam kaanch tootta nahi.\n4. (a) **Nahi**: 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄, gas namak ban jaati hai. (b) **Haan**: CaO paani kheenchta hai, aur ammonia se reaction nahi karta (CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂). Jaanch: N 2 = 2, H 8 = 8, S 1, O 4 ✅.\n5. Urea ka M = 12 + 16 + 2 × (14 + 2) = 12 + 16 + 32 = **60**, nitrogen 28. 70 ÷ 28 × 60 = **150 kg**. Jaanch: 150 kg urea mein N = 150 × 28 ÷ 60 = 70 ✅.\n6. 120 kg urea mein N = 120 × 28 ÷ 60 = **56 kg**. NH₄NO₃ (M 80, N 28): 56 ÷ 28 × 80 = **160 kg**. Jaanch: 160 × 28 ÷ 80 = 56 ✅.\n7. (NH₄)₂SO₄ ka M 132; 33 ÷ 132 = **0.25 kmol**. NH₃ = 0.5 kmol × 17 = **8.5 kg**; H₂SO₄ = 0.25 × 98 = **24.5 kg**. Jaanch: 8.5 + 24.5 = 33 ✅.\n8. 23 ÷ 0.46 = **50 kg**. Jaanch: 50 × 0.46 = 23 ✅.\n9. 3.4 ÷ 17 = **0.2 mol**. NH₃ + HCl → NH₄Cl (1 : 1 : 1). HCl = 0.2 × 36.5 = **7.3 g**; NH₄Cl = 0.2 × 53.5 = **10.7 g**. Jaanch: 3.4 + 7.3 = 10.7 ✅.\n10. 20.4 ÷ 17 = 1.2 mol NH₃. O₂ = 1.2 × 3 ÷ 4 = 0.9 mol, volume = 0.9 × 22.4 = **20.16 L**. Jaanch: O₂ = 0.9 × 32 = 28.8 g; N₂ = 0.6 mol = 16.8 g; H₂O = 1.8 mol = 32.4 g; 20.4 + 28.8 = 49.2 = 16.8 + 32.4 ✅.\n11. 51 ÷ 17 = **3 kmol** NH₃. N₂ = 1.5 kmol × 28 = **42 kg**; H₂ = 4.5 kmol × 2 = **9 kg**. Jaanch: 42 + 9 = 51 ✅. 100 °C par reaction bahut dheemi, isliye factory ke liye bekaar; garam karne par tezi aati hai par ammonia ka hissa ghatta hai: isliye samjhauta, lagbhag 450 °C aur iron catalyst.\n12. **Ulta jar** (mooh neeche), tube **upar tak**, kyunki ammonia hawa se halki hai: downward displacement of air. Paani ke upar nahi, kyunki 1 volume paani mein lagbhag 700 volume NH₃ ghulti hai: gas jama nahi hogi, aur paani jar mein tezi se chadh jaayega.\n13. (a) **False** ❌: conc. H₂SO₄ ammonia ko namak bana deta hai; CaO use karte hain. (b) **True** ✅. (c) **False** ❌: catalyst sirf speed badhata hai. (d) **False** ❌: sookhi NH₃ sookhe litmus par asar nahi karti; moist red litmus neela hota hai. (e) **True** ✅: NH₃ + HCl → NH₄Cl, 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄, NH₃ + HNO₃ → NH₄NO₃.\n\n---\n\nNetra ne ghar ja kar apni copy mein ek chhota sa chart banaya: \"hawa ka N₂ → NH₃ → khaad → khet\". Mr. Khadilkar ne kaha, \"Shabaash! Ab ye yaad rakhna ki ek gas ka dry karne ka tareeka uski prakriti dekhkar chuna jaata hai, naam dekhkar nahi.\"\n\n**Aage kya?** Is ammonia ko jab garam platinum ke upar oxygen milti hai to 4NH₃ + 5O₂ → 4NO + 6H₂O wali reaction hoti hai, aur NO se ek bahut shaktishali acid banta hai: nitric acid. Wo kaise banta hai aur sone ko bhi kaise gala deta hai: Topic 3 mein.",
            "bodyHinglish": "(Mass: H 1, C 12, N 14, O 16, S 32, Cl 35.5, Ca 40. Molar volume 22.4 L at STP.)\n\n1. A teacher heats 42.8 g of NH₄Cl with enough Ca(OH)₂. Find the mass of Ca(OH)₂ used, the mass of CaCl₂ formed, and the volume of NH₃ at STP.\n2. What mass of NH₄Cl must be heated with excess Ca(OH)₂ to obtain 6.72 L of ammonia at STP?\n3. Explain why the test tube used to prepare ammonia from NH₄Cl and Ca(OH)₂ is tilted with its mouth slightly downward.\n4. Ammonia is passed through each of (a) conc. H₂SO₄, (b) quicklime. For each, say whether ammonia is dried and write any equation.\n5. How many kg of urea contain 70 kg of nitrogen? (Use the formula CO(NH₂)₂.)\n6. A farmer needs the same amount of nitrogen as is present in 120 kg of urea, but wants to use NH₄NO₃ instead. How many kg of NH₄NO₃ is needed?\n7. How many kg of NH₃ and of H₂SO₄ are needed to make 33 kg of (NH₄)₂SO₄ by 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄?\n8. A bag of fertiliser is labelled \"N 46 percent\". A field needs 23 kg of nitrogen. How many kg of that fertiliser is needed?\n9. 3.4 g of NH₃ reacts completely with HCl gas to form white fumes. Find the mass of HCl used and the mass of NH₄Cl formed.\n10. 20.4 g of NH₃ burns completely in oxygen as 4NH₃ + 3O₂ → 2N₂ + 6H₂O. Find the volume of oxygen used at STP.\n11. In a Haber plant, 51 kg of NH₃ is made by N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃ (ideal case). Find the masses of N₂ and H₂ used. Then explain why plants run at about 450 °C and not at 100 °C, given that \"a lower temperature gives a larger share of ammonia in the mixture but the reaction becomes very slow\".\n12. Choose and justify: which gas jar position (upright or inverted) and which method collects ammonia, and why can it not be collected over water? What would be seen if a student tried?\n13. State True or False and correct the false ones: (a) Ammonia is dried with conc. H₂SO₄. (b) NH₃ is lighter than air. (c) A catalyst increases the amount of ammonia in the Haber mixture. (d) Dry NH₃ turns dry red litmus blue. (e) NH₄Cl, (NH₄)₂SO₄ and NH₄NO₃ are all made from ammonia.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. NH₄Cl = 53.5 g/mol, 42.8 ÷ 53.5 = **0.8 mol**. Ratio 2 : 1 : 1 : 2: Ca(OH)₂ = 0.4 mol × 74 = **29.6 g**; CaCl₂ = 0.4 × 111 = **44.4 g**; NH₃ = 0.8 mol, 0.8 × 22.4 = **17.92 L**. Jaanch: H₂O = 0.8 mol = 14.4 g, NH₃ = 0.8 × 17 = 13.6 g; reactants 42.8 + 29.6 = 72.4; products 44.4 + 14.4 + 13.6 = 72.4 ✅.\n2. 6.72 ÷ 22.4 = **0.3 mol** NH₃. Ratio 1 : 1 to NH₄Cl, to 0.3 mol = 0.3 × 53.5 = **16.05 g**. Jaanch: 16.05 ÷ 53.5 = 0.3 ✅.\n3. Reaction mein paani banta hai jo test tube ke thande mooh par boond bankar wapas garam tale ki taraf behne ki koshish karta hai. Mooh neeche hone se wo bahar nikal jaata hai aur garam kaanch tootta nahi.\n4. (a) **Nahi**: 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄, gas namak ban jaati hai. (b) **Haan**: CaO paani kheenchta hai, aur ammonia se reaction nahi karta (CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂). Jaanch: N 2 = 2, H 8 = 8, S 1, O 4 ✅.\n5. Urea ka M = 12 + 16 + 2 × (14 + 2) = 12 + 16 + 32 = **60**, nitrogen 28. 70 ÷ 28 × 60 = **150 kg**. Jaanch: 150 kg urea mein N = 150 × 28 ÷ 60 = 70 ✅.\n6. 120 kg urea mein N = 120 × 28 ÷ 60 = **56 kg**. NH₄NO₃ (M 80, N 28): 56 ÷ 28 × 80 = **160 kg**. Jaanch: 160 × 28 ÷ 80 = 56 ✅.\n7. (NH₄)₂SO₄ ka M 132; 33 ÷ 132 = **0.25 kmol**. NH₃ = 0.5 kmol × 17 = **8.5 kg**; H₂SO₄ = 0.25 × 98 = **24.5 kg**. Jaanch: 8.5 + 24.5 = 33 ✅.\n8. 23 ÷ 0.46 = **50 kg**. Jaanch: 50 × 0.46 = 23 ✅.\n9. 3.4 ÷ 17 = **0.2 mol**. NH₃ + HCl → NH₄Cl (1 : 1 : 1). HCl = 0.2 × 36.5 = **7.3 g**; NH₄Cl = 0.2 × 53.5 = **10.7 g**. Jaanch: 3.4 + 7.3 = 10.7 ✅.\n10. 20.4 ÷ 17 = 1.2 mol NH₃. O₂ = 1.2 × 3 ÷ 4 = 0.9 mol, volume = 0.9 × 22.4 = **20.16 L**. Jaanch: O₂ = 0.9 × 32 = 28.8 g; N₂ = 0.6 mol = 16.8 g; H₂O = 1.8 mol = 32.4 g; 20.4 + 28.8 = 49.2 = 16.8 + 32.4 ✅.\n11. 51 ÷ 17 = **3 kmol** NH₃. N₂ = 1.5 kmol × 28 = **42 kg**; H₂ = 4.5 kmol × 2 = **9 kg**. Jaanch: 42 + 9 = 51 ✅. 100 °C par reaction bahut dheemi, isliye factory ke liye bekaar; garam karne par tezi aati hai par ammonia ka hissa ghatta hai: isliye samjhauta, lagbhag 450 °C aur iron catalyst.\n12. **Ulta jar** (mooh neeche), tube **upar tak**, kyunki ammonia hawa se halki hai: downward displacement of air. Paani ke upar nahi, kyunki 1 volume paani mein lagbhag 700 volume NH₃ ghulti hai: gas jama nahi hogi, aur paani jar mein tezi se chadh jaayega.\n13. (a) **False** ❌: conc. H₂SO₄ ammonia ko namak bana deta hai; CaO use karte hain. (b) **True** ✅. (c) **False** ❌: catalyst sirf speed badhata hai. (d) **False** ❌: sookhi NH₃ sookhe litmus par asar nahi karti; moist red litmus neela hota hai. (e) **True** ✅: NH₃ + HCl → NH₄Cl, 2NH₃ + H₂SO₄ → (NH₄)₂SO₄, NH₃ + HNO₃ → NH₄NO₃.\n\n---\n\nNetra ne ghar ja kar apni copy mein ek chhota sa chart banaya: \"hawa ka N₂ → NH₃ → khaad → khet\". Mr. Khadilkar ne kaha, \"Shabaash! Ab ye yaad rakhna ki ek gas ka dry karne ka tareeka uski prakriti dekhkar chuna jaata hai, naam dekhkar nahi.\"\n\n**Aage kya?** Is ammonia ko jab garam platinum ke upar oxygen milti hai to 4NH₃ + 5O₂ → 4NO + 6H₂O wali reaction hoti hai, aur NO se ek bahut shaktishali acid banta hai: nitric acid. Wo kaise banta hai aur sone ko bhi kaise gala deta hai: Topic 3 mein."
          }
