            "headingHinglish": "Angithi, pencil aur heere ki angoothi",
            "body": "December ki thandi shaam thi. Mr. Dhaygude ne aangan ke khule kone mein purani **koyle ki angithi** jalayi thi, haath sekne ke liye. Unki bhanji Gayatri school ka kaam copy mein kar rahi thi, aur beech-beech mein apne thande haath angithi ki taraf badha kar sek leti thi. Mr. Dhaygude ne akhbaar ka ek panna uthaya: poore panne par **heere ki angoothi** ka vigyapan tha, chamakdar, bina rang ka patthar.\n\nGayatri ne apni pencil box se pencil nikali, nok ko ungli par ghisa to ungli kaali ho gayi. Phir usne angithi ke koyle ko dekha, jo bhi kaala tha, aur akhbaar ke heere ko dekha. \"Mama, ye teen cheezein ek jaisi kaise ho sakti hain? Koyla kaala aur bhurbhura hai, pencil ki nok kaali aur chikni hai, aur heera ek dum bina rang ka aur itna kadak ki sheeshe ko kaat de. Vigyapan ke neeche likha hai 'heera shuddh carbon se bana hai'. Ye to galat chhapa hoga!\"\n\nMr. Dhaygude hans pade. \"Bahut accha sawaal. Par vigyapan galat nahi hai. Koyla, pencil ki nok aur heera, teeno mein **wahi ek tatva** hai: carbon. Fark kisi aur tatva ka nahi hai, fark **carbon ke atomon ke jude hone ke tareeke** ka hai. Aur isi wajah se carbon ke saath aur bhi kai kamaal jude hain: cheeni, sabun, petrol, plastic, tumhari copy ka kaagaz. Chalo, pehle dekhte hain ki carbon mein aisa kya khaas hai.\"\n\nEk aur baat: angithi mein koyla jal raha tha, aur Mr. Dhaygude ne use **aangan mein khule mein** rakha tha, kamre ke andar nahi. Gayatri ne poocha kyun, to wo bole: \"Ye baat aage Suraksha wale box mein, pehle wahi padh lo.\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "December ki thandi shaam thi. Mr. Dhaygude ne aangan ke khule kone mein purani **koyle ki angithi** jalayi thi, haath sekne ke liye. Unki bhanji Gayatri school ka kaam copy mein kar rahi thi, aur beech-beech mein apne thande haath angithi ki taraf badha kar sek leti thi. Mr. Dhaygude ne akhbaar ka ek panna uthaya: poore panne par **heere ki angoothi** ka vigyapan tha, chamakdar, bina rang ka patthar.\n\nGayatri ne apni pencil box se pencil nikali, nok ko ungli par ghisa to ungli kaali ho gayi. Phir usne angithi ke koyle ko dekha, jo bhi kaala tha, aur akhbaar ke heere ko dekha. \"Mama, ye teen cheezein ek jaisi kaise ho sakti hain? Koyla kaala aur bhurbhura hai, pencil ki nok kaali aur chikni hai, aur heera ek dum bina rang ka aur itna kadak ki sheeshe ko kaat de. Vigyapan ke neeche likha hai 'heera shuddh carbon se bana hai'. Ye to galat chhapa hoga!\"\n\nMr. Dhaygude hans pade. \"Bahut accha sawaal. Par vigyapan galat nahi hai. Koyla, pencil ki nok aur heera, teeno mein **wahi ek tatva** hai: carbon. Fark kisi aur tatva ka nahi hai, fark **carbon ke atomon ke jude hone ke tareeke** ka hai. Aur isi wajah se carbon ke saath aur bhi kai kamaal jude hain: cheeni, sabun, petrol, plastic, tumhari copy ka kaagaz. Chalo, pehle dekhte hain ki carbon mein aisa kya khaas hai.\"\n\nEk aur baat: angithi mein koyla jal raha tha, aur Mr. Dhaygude ne use **aangan mein khule mein** rakha tha, kamre ke andar nahi. Gayatri ne poocha kyun, to wo bole: \"Ye baat aage Suraksha wale box mein, pehle wahi padh lo.\""
